WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.835
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.236
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:06.106
between Lay's and Walkers
in the US and the UK.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.640
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.343
We'll start with a quick note

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.678
to explain their different names.

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.013
Walkers used to be its own company

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:15.148
and was the most popular
crisp brand in the UK.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:17.650
Frito-Lay actually
acquired Walkers in 1989,

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.686
but they decided to still
use the brand name in the UK

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.621
so all that brand loyalty
didn't go to waste.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:24.324
In the UK, Walkers crisps
come in five portion sizes.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:26.226
A multipack 25-gram bag,

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:28.028
a 32.5-gram bag,

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:29.362
a 45-gram bag,

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:30.797
a 65-gram bag,

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.400
and a 175-gram sharing bag.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.237
The smallest that's in the
multipack bag is 28 grams.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.406
Then we move up to a 78-gram bag,

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:41.541
a 226-gram bag,

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:46.012
and then our party-size bag, 368 grams.

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:49.849
That means our biggest bag is 110% larger

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:52.318
than the biggest bag in the UK.

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:53.253
A few other things to note.

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.921
In the UK, if you get a flavored bag,

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:56.956
it's the same weight as
the ready-salted version.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.858
Whereas in the US, our flavored bags

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.593
weigh less than the
original-flavored bags.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:04.030
Take this bag of salt and vinegar chips.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.166
It weighs 7.75 ounces,

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:10.003
compared to the classic
regular-salted 8-ounce bag.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:13.073
Back in 2014, PepsiCo claimed the reason

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:15.208
there is a slightly higher price per ounce

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.577
for flavored chips is the added seasoning.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:19.312
OK, before we continue,

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.848
they're telling us,
"Weighs less, costs more

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:24.150
because we're adding more
seasoning." Right, guys?

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.453
Well, I got a question for you, PepsiCo.

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:27.887
[grunting]

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.155
What does that say there?

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.523
Says "Lightly Salted."

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:33.660
So I understand this has
less salt than these guys?

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.928
Huh.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:38.965
Closer inspection: right
there, 7 3/4 ounces.

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.300
Not the full 8.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.236
If there's less seasoning
and salt in here,

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:46.239
why is it a smaller
ounce and a higher price?

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:48.975
They're stealing my salt!

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:51.611
Salt, literally the cheapest
thing on the planet.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:53.146
We have a whole ocean full of it,

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.482
and yet they're still skimping on it!

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.785
Your move, PepsiCo.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:02.689
This 28-gram bag of chips
supposedly has 15 chips in it,

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.791
according to Lay's website.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.459
Well, they lied about the salt,

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.594
what else are they lying about?

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:08.428
I'm going to count the crisps

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:10.196
in this 25-gram bag for comparison.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.397
These chips are demolished.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.534
I feel like it's more than 15.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:15.802
This is what we call the

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:18.138
stoner-math section of "Food Wars."

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.373
We do the math so you
stoners don't have to.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.909
All right. So, one, two.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.477
That's a whole one.

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:25.345
Little peephole.

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:27.714
Absolute Frankenstein of a crisp, this.

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:31.718
Arguably not one
put-together chip in here.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:32.952
OK, let's just ...

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:35.655
that's a chip, that's a chip, right?

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:36.923
So, the issue there is that the crisps

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.625
are all vastly different sizes.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:41.261
Like, this one, just one
crisp, but it's tiny,

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:43.596
whereas this one, also
one crisp, but way bigger.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:46.032
And we've ended up with 22.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.201
Of all the arbitrary
things we do on this show,

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.903
this has to be the most arbitrary.

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:51.137
Wow, look at that, everyone!

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:52.639
They gave me an extra chip.

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:54.607
16 instead of 15.

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:55.542
The last thing we wanted to check

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:57.143
was how much air you're
getting in your bags.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.912
Walkers in the UK are kind of notorious

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.813
for seemingly underfilling the bags.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.448
We're going to find the volume of the bag

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:04.317
and then the volume of the crisps inside

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:06.386
to find out just how much
wasted space there is.

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:09.889
What I need to do is
carefully open the bag

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.057
just enough to let the air out,

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:13.293
and then I'm going to
try and powder these,

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:15.195
like just crush them as far as I can,

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:18.131
and then measure the volume
of the powder in this thing.

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:21.401
First I gotta crumble it up.

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:23.002
[whispering] Crushing bags with Harry.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:25.538
[bag crackling]

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:28.208
Oh, this is like ... [growls].

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.244
It's quite therapeutic.

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:33.446
It feels like I'm giving a massage.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.315
Just, like, the world's worst massage.

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.454
I need something to kind of tamp it down,

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.489
'cause the air is stuck in
there, so I'll just use,

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:44.490
oh, I don't know,

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.192
this pair of nunchucks!

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.332
Oh, yeah!

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.735
Now, step two is going to be

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.403
to find the volume of the bag itself.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.239
So we're going to fill the bag with water

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.140
to try and find the volume.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.542
Oh, God. Oh.

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:03.810
Tiny bit more.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:04.611
Perfect.

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:06.512
Sarah: OK. We did it!

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.780
But now I have to get it in there

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.350
without spilling it everywhere.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.618
Three, two, one, go.

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:13.253
[laughing]

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.088
Sarah: Oh, that is perfect!

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:15.922
Harry: Look at that!

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:17.123
That went pretty well.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.891
We didn't spill water everywhere.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.328
Oh, my God, it's, like,
right to the top there.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.930
That's crazy how that worked. OK.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.932
Buchi and Wumi are making
a triumphant return.

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:28.234
Go and watch the Oreos episode
if you haven't already.

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:30.970
Some of that,

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.339
and then measure the rest.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.441
Y'all brought number two!

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:38.344
[laughing] Oh, God.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.580
Can you see the bits of stuff
floating around in there?

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:41.881
So, according to my trusted friend

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:43.416
PercentageCalculator.net,

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:47.687
around 90% of a 25-gram
Walkers bag is wasted space.

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:48.921
I don't know what the math is

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:51.224
I'm supposed to be figuring out, I forgot,

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:54.661
but whoever's editing this,
take all those numbers,

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:56.963
and this is the conclusion.

00:04:56.963 --> 00:05:00.233
Now, that air is actually
there for a reason.

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:02.669
It's nitrogen gas, which
helps preserve the chips

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:03.903
and also acts as a cushion

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:06.072
to stop them getting smashed in transit.

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:07.607
I mean, imagine what it'd be like

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:08.841
if it didn't have all that air in there.

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:11.010
So, as much air as there is in there,

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.111
it's actually vitally important.

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:13.646
If anything, they should put
more air in these things,

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.715
'cause these things, they turn into dust.

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:17.016
Into dust!

00:05:18.618 --> 00:05:20.253
Here are all the Walkers
products from the UK

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:21.854
that you won't find in the US.

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:24.557
And here is everything
you can only get in the US

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:26.059
and not in the UK.

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:29.228
I am losing my mind, let's go!

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.129
I want to start with a couple

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:32.131
of linguistic/stylistic differences

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:33.232
rather than anything else.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:34.967
For example, in the UK,

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:37.837
we call our classic Walkers ready salted,

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:39.272
as opposed to original.

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:43.376
I believe this is a reference
to the very old days of crisps

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:44.610
where what you would actually get

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.412
is just, like, a bag of plain crisps,

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:48.081
and then you would have
to add your own salt.

00:05:48.081 --> 00:05:49.449
These ones are ready salted.

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:51.050
You don't have to add any
salt, it's already on there.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.685
One stylistic difference
that's worth pointing out

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:55.955
is that in the UK, our salt
and vinegar chips are green.

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:59.525
I will say Walkers is kind of
the only brand that does that.

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:01.327
And then we're on to some
actual exclusive flavors.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:04.230
We'll start with this one,
which is cheese and onion.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.698
Now, Americans don't
have cheese and onion,

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.166
which might shock a few Brits

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:08.701
because it's one of the
most popular flavors here.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:11.170
Instead they have I think,
like, cheddar and sour cream

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.538
and sour cream and onion.

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:13.773
It just ruins your breath.

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:15.708
Your breath smells so bad after these.

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:17.143
How did I get so lucky?

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:19.312
I love chips, I love different flavors,

00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:21.748
I love trying new varieties,
and I hate paying for it.

00:06:21.748 --> 00:06:24.016
So this is perfect for me.

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.585
I'm going to start with a flavor

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:28.121
that I never even heard
of, cheddar jalapeño.

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:31.424
Oh, my God!

00:06:32.692 --> 00:06:34.127
I like the kick on these.

00:06:34.127 --> 00:06:35.862
It reminds me of the
cheddar and sour cream,

00:06:35.862 --> 00:06:37.296
which I can't believe you guys don't have.

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:40.500
This flavor took over about 20 years ago,

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:43.870
and I don't know why it's
so good, but it is good!

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:44.737
Love this flavor.

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:45.571
If I had to rank them though,

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:47.407
I'll put the jalapeño above that one,

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:48.608
the cheddar and sour cream.

00:06:48.608 --> 00:06:50.042
Sour cream and onion, I
don't even got to open these.

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:52.044
Sour cream and onion, classic flavor.

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:54.580
I mean, barbecue in America is amazing.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.883
I mean, this is just a
classic, classic flavor.

00:06:58.484 --> 00:06:59.919
Oh, man. Fantastic.

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:03.556
But how does that compare to
sweet Southern heat barbecue?

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:05.024
Southern heat!

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:07.593
Oh, yeah.

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:08.961
I put these above these.

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.363
Then we got honey barbecue.

00:07:10.363 --> 00:07:11.931
How sweet is this one going to be?

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:14.901
You got greedy with the sweetness.

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:16.302
Ooh, chili lime.

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:18.070
Yeah, dude. I've never had these before.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.472
Chilies and limes.

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:20.673
See that? Chilies, limes.

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:22.275
Fantastic combination.

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:24.944
Ooh, I don't know how I feel about these.

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:26.212
It's like, I wasn't into them before,

00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:27.580
but now I kind of can't stop eating them.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:28.781
Another iconic British flavor

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.983
that's also exclusive is prawn cocktail.

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:33.152
Brits became really
obsessed with prawn cocktail

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:35.054
in, like, the '70s, I think it was.

00:07:35.054 --> 00:07:36.622
It just became a sort of trendy thing

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:37.890
to serve at dinner parties.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.859
I'm not mad about that, because
it is a really tasty one.

00:07:39.859 --> 00:07:41.928
It just kind of tastes tomatoey,

00:07:41.928 --> 00:07:43.629
because it was usually served with

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:46.933
a tomato mayo-Worcestershire
sauce combination.

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:48.701
Next we've got a personal
favorite of mine,

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:50.436
which is Marmite crisps.

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:52.371
God, I love Marmite. Marmite is fantastic.

00:07:52.371 --> 00:07:54.574
The slogan was, "You either
love it or you hate it,"

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:56.509
and it does still ring true,
I think, for most people.

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:57.910
I'm firmly in the love-it camp.

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:02.014
Bit of tang from the amount
of salt that's in there.

00:08:02.014 --> 00:08:03.082
Fantastic crisp.

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:06.452
Harry was nice enough to send
me some of his UK exclusives,

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:07.587
which I'm going to look at right now.

00:08:07.587 --> 00:08:08.488
Where do I want to start?

00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:10.523
I guess all start — oh, no.

00:08:10.523 --> 00:08:11.591
Marmite.

00:08:11.591 --> 00:08:13.659
I don't get why people love Marmite.

00:08:17.897 --> 00:08:19.365
Ugh!

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:22.668
I mean, it tastes exactly like ass.

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:23.636
I hear millennials like that,

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:24.971
so maybe that's a selling point for them.

00:08:24.971 --> 00:08:26.672
They should actually be
like, "Tastes like ass,"

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:30.343
'cause the kids are into that
these days, but I am not.

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:31.711
Then we have a couple of meaty options,

00:08:31.711 --> 00:08:33.913
which I'm surprised you guys
don't have in the States.

00:08:33.913 --> 00:08:36.282
We kind of love combining
crisps and meat, as it seems,

00:08:36.282 --> 00:08:39.218
starting with these roast chicken crisps.

00:08:39.218 --> 00:08:42.188
Another meaty option is
these, which is smoky bacon.

00:08:42.188 --> 00:08:43.489
Then we have these ones,

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:45.725
which are tomato-ketchup-flavored Walkers.

00:08:47.793 --> 00:08:50.663
In my opinion, prawn cocktail does ketchup

00:08:50.663 --> 00:08:52.031
better than ketchup does ketchup.

00:08:52.031 --> 00:08:53.933
And then for the last of
our standard crisp flavors,

00:08:53.933 --> 00:08:54.967
we have pickled onion.

00:08:54.967 --> 00:08:55.868
Pickled onion's another thing

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:57.236
that's kind of iconic to British culture

00:08:57.236 --> 00:08:59.739
in the same way that maybe
prawn cocktail or Marmite are,

00:08:59.739 --> 00:09:00.773
just 'cause it's quite traditional

00:09:00.773 --> 00:09:03.976
to find a big jar of pickled
onions or pickled eggs in pubs,

00:09:03.976 --> 00:09:05.611
and you'd have one of those as a bar snack

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:06.646
while you're drinking your pint.

00:09:08.281 --> 00:09:10.049
The complaint I often have against pickles

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:12.051
and pickled onions is that
they're not tangy enough.

00:09:12.051 --> 00:09:14.587
And these are very tangy,
so good job, Walkers.

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.191
Puckering pickled onion.

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:20.593
What does that mean?

00:09:20.593 --> 00:09:23.262
Puckering? Like [makes kissing sound]?

00:09:23.262 --> 00:09:26.766
Like I'm being kissed by a pickled onion?

00:09:26.766 --> 00:09:28.100
Yo, these suck!

00:09:29.135 --> 00:09:30.503
Hey, Joe, can I try some of those?

00:09:30.503 --> 00:09:33.172
Hey, Harry, try some of
these great American flavors!

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:39.612
Thank you!

00:09:40.646 --> 00:09:41.647
Let's start with the limón.

00:09:41.647 --> 00:09:42.949
That's what I've got in my hand.

00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:48.621
Ooh, those are lemony!

00:09:48.621 --> 00:09:49.455
Whew!

00:09:49.455 --> 00:09:50.856
I don't think I've ever
had a citrus crisp before.

00:09:50.856 --> 00:09:52.224
That is not something
that we have in the UK.

00:09:52.224 --> 00:09:53.159
Those are good.

00:09:53.159 --> 00:09:55.995
I gotta say, love these chips.

00:09:55.995 --> 00:09:56.963
Yeah.

00:09:56.963 --> 00:09:58.497
I got to score a bag of these.

00:09:58.497 --> 00:10:02.802
Chesapeake Bay crab seasoning Lay's.

00:10:03.903 --> 00:10:05.638
Uh-oh!

00:10:05.638 --> 00:10:06.472
Yuelei: No?

00:10:06.472 --> 00:10:08.240
Yeah, no, these are bad.
Put these at the bottom.

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:10.776
These are at my 7-Eleven.

00:10:10.776 --> 00:10:13.112
Tomato-and-chili-flavored
chips, which sounds amazing.

00:10:13.112 --> 00:10:15.948
I'm going to pronounce
this wrong. Sabritas?

00:10:15.948 --> 00:10:17.383
Adobadas.

00:10:17.383 --> 00:10:18.584
"Hecho en Mexico."

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:22.021
Oh, yeah, dude!

00:10:22.021 --> 00:10:23.322
Not that spicy. They remind me kind of

00:10:23.322 --> 00:10:24.991
a little bit like Takis.

00:10:24.991 --> 00:10:26.092
Look how red this is.

00:10:26.092 --> 00:10:27.893
Don't you think they'd be super spicy?

00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:28.728
I like that.

00:10:28.728 --> 00:10:29.629
These chip brands,

00:10:29.629 --> 00:10:31.130
they're all going after
each other's throats.

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:34.500
It is really just like guerrilla warfare.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.202
You guys don't understand what's going on

00:10:36.202 --> 00:10:37.970
in our grocery stores in this country.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:41.774
This is an uneasy mafia
alliance in Chip City.

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.846
No.

00:10:46.846 --> 00:10:49.115
Because when it's thin like these,

00:10:49.115 --> 00:10:50.683
it brings out the flavor more,

00:10:50.683 --> 00:10:52.485
if that makes sense, and it's too strong.

00:10:54.453 --> 00:10:56.255
It turns out if you put
Doritos Cool Ranch seasoning

00:10:56.255 --> 00:10:57.590
on anything, it'll taste good.

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.358
Dill pickle.

00:10:59.358 --> 00:11:00.626
So, I hate pickles.

00:11:00.626 --> 00:11:01.661
Oof.

00:11:04.797 --> 00:11:07.033
[groaning]

00:11:07.033 --> 00:11:07.967
I hate them!

00:11:07.967 --> 00:11:09.835
Put these at the bottom of every list.

00:11:09.835 --> 00:11:11.771
I don't know what the
Flamin' Hot dill pickle chips

00:11:11.771 --> 00:11:13.839
taste like, but the
regular dill pickle chips

00:11:13.839 --> 00:11:15.508
are absolutely disgusting.

00:11:15.508 --> 00:11:17.009
These sound phenomenal.

00:11:17.009 --> 00:11:19.512
Flamin' Hot dill-pickle-flavored crisps.

00:11:22.381 --> 00:11:23.582
Match made in heaven for me.

00:11:23.582 --> 00:11:25.651
You get the heat, you get
that little bit of tang

00:11:25.651 --> 00:11:27.186
to kind of cut through it.

00:11:27.186 --> 00:11:28.621
If I could take one of these four

00:11:28.621 --> 00:11:31.757
and have them in the UK
permanently, these ones.

00:11:31.757 --> 00:11:33.392
One thing Walkers utilize a lot in the UK

00:11:33.392 --> 00:11:34.760
are promotional flavors.

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:36.062
So currently what they've got going on

00:11:36.062 --> 00:11:36.996
is one where they've partnered

00:11:36.996 --> 00:11:38.798
with four different
restaurants from around the UK

00:11:38.798 --> 00:11:40.533
to showcase some different cuisines.

00:11:40.533 --> 00:11:42.068
So that means that we now have

00:11:42.068 --> 00:11:43.703
fish-and-chip-flavored Walkers,

00:11:43.703 --> 00:11:45.671
Madras-curry-flavored Walkers,

00:11:45.671 --> 00:11:47.339
Thai-green-curry-flavored Walkers,

00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:49.141
and chicken burrito Walkers.

00:11:49.141 --> 00:11:51.944
At one point they made
a Cajun squirrel flavor.

00:11:51.944 --> 00:11:52.945
I'm not making that up.

00:11:52.945 --> 00:11:55.881
This one looks really
good. Thai green curry?

00:11:55.881 --> 00:11:57.516
Think I'm gonna like this.

00:11:58.684 --> 00:12:00.786
Yuck. Yuck!

00:12:00.786 --> 00:12:01.754
Rank them down.

00:12:01.754 --> 00:12:02.655
Fish and chips. OK.

00:12:02.655 --> 00:12:04.156
I like fish and chips. Hang on.

00:12:04.156 --> 00:12:05.558
It smells like cat food.

00:12:05.558 --> 00:12:07.760
Now I can't stop thinking
about dry cat food.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.195
All right. I like fish and chips.

00:12:15.201 --> 00:12:16.769
This is the worst one.

00:12:16.769 --> 00:12:18.137
This is so — [choking].

00:12:18.137 --> 00:12:19.171
I'm gonna throw up.

00:12:20.573 --> 00:12:24.276
Crown it. This is the
worst chip I've ever eaten,

00:12:24.276 --> 00:12:25.945
the worst chip I've ever reviewed,

00:12:25.945 --> 00:12:28.814
and this might be the worst
thing I've ever tasted.

00:12:28.814 --> 00:12:30.850
Like, I feel like I'm on a prank show.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.485
"We farted in a bag, gotcha!"

00:12:32.485 --> 00:12:34.220
Like, oh, you know, like —

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:36.255
In the UK, Walkers has
a range of Baked crisps,

00:12:36.255 --> 00:12:37.189
which I guess are marketed as

00:12:37.189 --> 00:12:38.524
kind of like a healthier option.

00:12:38.524 --> 00:12:39.992
These come in four flavors:

00:12:39.992 --> 00:12:42.962
salt and vinegar, cheese and onion,

00:12:42.962 --> 00:12:46.232
sour cream and onion, prawn cocktail.

00:12:46.232 --> 00:12:48.100
We also have Baked potato chip options,

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:49.502
and one Baked flavor you can get here

00:12:49.502 --> 00:12:53.672
you can't get it in the UK
is this, the barbecue Baked.

00:12:53.672 --> 00:12:54.507
Besides the Baked,

00:12:54.507 --> 00:12:56.475
there are also these
other healthier options

00:12:56.475 --> 00:12:58.477
for Lay's potato chips fans.

00:12:58.477 --> 00:13:01.847
It's known as the Better for
You range of potato chips,

00:13:01.847 --> 00:13:02.848
and you can't get them in the UK.

00:13:02.848 --> 00:13:05.551
You can get them here in
the US, including these,

00:13:05.551 --> 00:13:08.354
the before-mentioned lightly salted chips.

00:13:08.354 --> 00:13:10.990
Besides these, you can get
lightly salted barbecue,

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:14.960
wavy lightly salted,
Simply sea salt thick-cut,

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:16.829
and Simply barbecue thick-cut.

00:13:16.829 --> 00:13:19.198
If you like crunchy chips,
Lay's also has you covered.

00:13:19.198 --> 00:13:21.534
They have their Kettle Cooked series.

00:13:21.534 --> 00:13:24.370
Here's four of the
flavors that I could find.

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:25.604
Original.

00:13:25.604 --> 00:13:27.740
Flamin' Hot. You guys
want me to open these?

00:13:29.375 --> 00:13:30.743
[laughing]

00:13:30.743 --> 00:13:31.911
These are so red.

00:13:31.911 --> 00:13:33.546
These win the reddest-chip award.

00:13:33.546 --> 00:13:34.446
Look how red these are.

00:13:34.446 --> 00:13:36.615
Like my eyes. Ahh!

00:13:38.617 --> 00:13:40.386
I like the flavor of these,
but they're not very hot.

00:13:40.386 --> 00:13:41.954
Oh, wait, yeah, they are. Ooh, yeah.

00:13:41.954 --> 00:13:44.290
Oh, man, the Kettle Cooked jalapeño.

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:45.591
I think this whole kettle-chip thing

00:13:45.591 --> 00:13:47.560
was just a ruse to go after Miss Vickie's.

00:13:49.728 --> 00:13:51.530
Yep. They're, like, really similar.

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:52.998
And I love those Miss Vickie chips.

00:13:52.998 --> 00:13:54.266
Sea salt and vinegar.

00:13:54.266 --> 00:13:56.468
Sea salt and cracked pepper.

00:13:56.468 --> 00:13:58.504
Other Kettle Cooked flavors
I could not get my hands on

00:13:58.504 --> 00:14:01.340
include the mesquite
barbecue, the Maui onion —

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:02.741
oh, I would have loved those —

00:14:02.741 --> 00:14:05.344
and, of course, the reduced-fat original.

00:14:05.344 --> 00:14:06.178
Sorry.

00:14:06.178 --> 00:14:08.514
We'll start with this one,
which is Max Punchy Paprika.

00:14:08.514 --> 00:14:09.882
Now, I'm surprised you
guys don't have more

00:14:09.882 --> 00:14:11.450
paprika-flavored crisps in the US,

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:12.551
'cause it's a really good flavor.

00:14:12.551 --> 00:14:13.652
I like how they have a

00:14:13.652 --> 00:14:16.121
"not actual size" warning on this bag,

00:14:16.121 --> 00:14:18.090
just in case you thought that one crisp

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:20.059
was the size of your head as well.

00:14:20.059 --> 00:14:23.395
Next up we've got Sizzling
Flame-Grilled Steak Max crisps.

00:14:23.395 --> 00:14:24.496
Now, these ones I'm interested by.

00:14:24.496 --> 00:14:25.865
These are Max crisps,

00:14:25.865 --> 00:14:29.301
and they are double
crunch KFC Zinger flavor.

00:14:29.301 --> 00:14:30.836
I think in the UK, we have a sort of

00:14:30.836 --> 00:14:33.072
hot chicken sandwich at
KFC called a Zinger burger,

00:14:33.072 --> 00:14:35.941
and supposedly these
are flavored like that.

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:40.579
Little Guy Fieri flames on the chip there.

00:14:40.579 --> 00:14:41.447
Yeah, pretty good.

00:14:43.048 --> 00:14:45.184
See, the flavor is not very strong,

00:14:45.184 --> 00:14:47.486
but they're not kidding
on the double crunch.

00:14:47.486 --> 00:14:50.656
This is like [crunching],

00:14:50.656 --> 00:14:53.192
"I'm a man! I want to take
my crunching to the max!

00:14:53.192 --> 00:14:54.627
Bleh!" Like, this is —

00:14:54.627 --> 00:14:56.862
If the Zinger crisps somehow
weren't enough KFC for you,

00:14:56.862 --> 00:14:58.964
then we also just have a kind of standard

00:14:58.964 --> 00:15:01.300
KFC Max crisp as well.

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:04.236
The next one we have is this
Fiercely Flamin' Hot flavor.

00:15:04.236 --> 00:15:06.772
Then we've got a few Max Strong crisps,

00:15:06.772 --> 00:15:07.907
which I think are Walkers' attempt

00:15:07.907 --> 00:15:10.509
to market to quite a specific demographic,

00:15:10.509 --> 00:15:13.412
which is mostly male, a little bit older,

00:15:13.412 --> 00:15:16.181
and kind of, like, the
blokey, laddie types.

00:15:16.181 --> 00:15:18.817
And it says "perfect with
beer" underneath. Like ...

00:15:18.817 --> 00:15:20.352
Putting the marketing to
one side for a second,

00:15:20.352 --> 00:15:21.453
they come in three flavors,

00:15:21.453 --> 00:15:25.090
which are hot chicken
wings, fiery peri-peri,

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:26.558
and jalapeño and cheese.

00:15:26.558 --> 00:15:28.627
Then our final three Max
flavors are these three,

00:15:28.627 --> 00:15:30.496
which are loaded cheddar and onion,

00:15:30.496 --> 00:15:31.797
bold barbecue ribs,

00:15:31.797 --> 00:15:34.366
and XXL chicken and chorizo flavored.

00:15:34.366 --> 00:15:37.002
You can also get Lay's Wavy chips,

00:15:37.002 --> 00:15:39.338
which is their shameless
rip-off of Ruffles.

00:15:39.338 --> 00:15:41.173
And with Wavys, they come in flavors

00:15:41.173 --> 00:15:42.908
of reduced-fat original;

00:15:42.908 --> 00:15:44.376
original, which I think are these;

00:15:44.376 --> 00:15:45.744
I brought the ranch!

00:15:45.744 --> 00:15:48.347
Hickory barbecue, salt and
pepper, and lightly salted,

00:15:48.347 --> 00:15:49.949
and one that I think is limited,

00:15:49.949 --> 00:15:51.317
because it says on the bag.

00:15:51.317 --> 00:15:52.384
Look what I found.

00:15:52.384 --> 00:15:54.753
I don't even think
Harry knows I got these.

00:15:54.753 --> 00:15:58.357
Carnitas street tacos Wavys.

00:15:58.357 --> 00:16:00.426
Hell yes.

00:16:00.426 --> 00:16:03.629
Whoa, smells good.

00:16:04.463 --> 00:16:05.764
Oh, smells real good, actually.

00:16:07.399 --> 00:16:08.934
Uh-oh. These aren't that good.

00:16:08.934 --> 00:16:12.705
Trying to get flavored carnitas and onion

00:16:12.705 --> 00:16:14.740
and cilantro and lime

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:16.342
all in a chip is very difficult.

00:16:16.342 --> 00:16:18.544
Good effort, guys, good
attempt, but I mean ...

00:16:18.544 --> 00:16:19.812
Next up we've got Sensations,

00:16:19.812 --> 00:16:22.815
which is Walkers' range of
slightly more upmarket crisps.

00:16:22.815 --> 00:16:24.950
They come with this very
sleek black packaging.

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:28.020
They have the kind of slightly
fancier flavor descriptions.

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:29.955
So, the classic Sensations
come in four flavors,

00:16:29.955 --> 00:16:30.889
which are as follows:

00:16:30.889 --> 00:16:33.859
got this one, which is
hickory-smoked cheddar and bacon.

00:16:33.859 --> 00:16:35.794
This one, which is
roasted chicken and thyme,

00:16:35.794 --> 00:16:36.862
personal favorite of mine.

00:16:36.862 --> 00:16:38.530
And we've got this one,
which is balsamic vinegar

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:39.898
and caramelized onion.

00:16:39.898 --> 00:16:41.633
And a firm crowd favorite on the end here,

00:16:41.633 --> 00:16:43.602
which is Thai sweet chili Sensations.

00:16:43.602 --> 00:16:45.270
Now, finally, Sensations also offer these

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.373
lime and coriander chutney Poppadoms.

00:16:47.373 --> 00:16:49.174
Also in the US you can
get something called Stax,

00:16:49.174 --> 00:16:51.377
which is this. It's not
so much, I don't think,

00:16:51.377 --> 00:16:55.614
unique flavors, it's just
a different chip vessel.

00:16:55.614 --> 00:16:57.816
Clearly, Lay's is going after Pringles.

00:16:57.816 --> 00:16:59.318
I mean, they're all
going after each other.

00:16:59.318 --> 00:17:02.154
These chip brands, man,
they are cutthroat.

00:17:02.154 --> 00:17:04.857
Let's find out how good of a job

00:17:04.857 --> 00:17:07.393
the Stax do

00:17:07.393 --> 00:17:10.763
protecting their chips.

00:17:10.763 --> 00:17:12.998
Did that really do that good of a job

00:17:12.998 --> 00:17:14.600
protecting these chips?

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:16.201
They're still, some of them are broken.

00:17:16.201 --> 00:17:18.771
Ooh, Buffalo wings with ranch. All right.

00:17:18.771 --> 00:17:20.973
Xtra Flamin' Hot, Yuelei.

00:17:20.973 --> 00:17:22.441
Ready to turn it up?

00:17:24.209 --> 00:17:25.377
Surely you jest.

00:17:25.377 --> 00:17:26.578
These are not spicy at all.

00:17:26.578 --> 00:17:27.880
Whoa, major letdown.

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:31.316
That's Xtra Flamin' Hot,
and this is Flamas Xtreme.

00:17:31.316 --> 00:17:34.219
But different colors, and
it's worded differently.

00:17:34.219 --> 00:17:35.521
Jesus.

00:17:35.521 --> 00:17:37.089
If you saw this color in the wild,

00:17:37.089 --> 00:17:39.158
you're in trouble. Turn around and run.

00:17:39.158 --> 00:17:41.026
Spicy Chile Limón.

00:17:41.026 --> 00:17:44.096
It's like, how do we make our
chips worse on your palate

00:17:44.096 --> 00:17:45.631
and worse for the environment?

00:17:45.631 --> 00:17:47.666
Ta-da. Stax were born.

00:17:47.666 --> 00:17:48.500
Avoid.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.402
Other flavors I was not
able to get my hands on

00:17:50.402 --> 00:17:53.172
by time of filming this: bacon
and cheddar potato skins,

00:17:53.172 --> 00:17:55.908
mesquite barbecue, and Flamas.

00:17:55.908 --> 00:17:59.211
Poppables, which is them
going after Doritos 3D,

00:17:59.211 --> 00:18:02.114
and Doritos 3D was just
Doritos going after Bugles.

00:18:02.114 --> 00:18:03.482
They got four flavors.

00:18:03.482 --> 00:18:05.350
I got all four. I can't believe it.

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:08.120
Those flavors are sea salt,

00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:09.321
sea salt and vinegar.

00:18:09.321 --> 00:18:12.024
Yo, what's up?! Salty!

00:18:12.024 --> 00:18:13.592
Honey barbecue.

00:18:13.592 --> 00:18:14.793
White cheddar.

00:18:14.793 --> 00:18:17.329
I don't want to try these at
all, but I feel like I should.

00:18:17.329 --> 00:18:19.198
What is this?

00:18:19.198 --> 00:18:21.733
It's like a little, like, chip pod.

00:18:23.368 --> 00:18:25.070
What is the point of this?

00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:26.472
I don't like Poppables.

00:18:27.873 --> 00:18:29.108
We do have Stax in the UK,

00:18:29.108 --> 00:18:30.943
but they're marketed under
the Doritos brand name

00:18:30.943 --> 00:18:32.444
rather than the Walkers brand name.

00:18:32.444 --> 00:18:33.645
We also used to have Poppables,

00:18:33.645 --> 00:18:35.447
but it seems like they've
recently been discontinued.

00:18:35.447 --> 00:18:37.216
That said, we do have a bunch
of other exclusive snacks

00:18:37.216 --> 00:18:38.817
marketed under the Walkers brand name.

00:18:38.817 --> 00:18:39.918
We'll start with Wotsits,

00:18:39.918 --> 00:18:42.221
which I think are like
our equivalent of Cheetos.

00:18:42.221 --> 00:18:43.722
We used to be able to
get Cheetos in the UK,

00:18:43.722 --> 00:18:45.057
but then they got taken off the shelves.

00:18:45.057 --> 00:18:46.358
Basically what we have are these, like,

00:18:46.358 --> 00:18:48.861
baked cheesy puff snacks.

00:18:48.861 --> 00:18:50.062
The standard flavor is cheese,

00:18:50.062 --> 00:18:51.363
which is this blue one here,

00:18:51.363 --> 00:18:53.932
but they also come in
the form of Flamin' Hot.

00:18:53.932 --> 00:18:56.802
And you can get both flavors
either as a small version

00:18:56.802 --> 00:18:58.403
or as a giant version.

00:18:58.403 --> 00:18:59.505
Next up we've got Monster Munch,

00:18:59.505 --> 00:19:02.441
which are these kind of
puffed corn, maize snacks

00:19:02.441 --> 00:19:04.076
in the shape of a monster claw.

00:19:04.076 --> 00:19:04.910
And you can get them flavored

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:07.179
with either pickled onion, roast beef,

00:19:07.179 --> 00:19:08.113
or in Flamin' Hot,

00:19:08.113 --> 00:19:09.715
which unfortunately I couldn't find today.

00:19:09.715 --> 00:19:10.949
Just like Wotsits, you can get them

00:19:10.949 --> 00:19:13.318
as the regular size or as the giant size.

00:19:13.318 --> 00:19:14.319
Next up we've got Quavers.

00:19:14.319 --> 00:19:17.556
These are kind of like a
thin, puffed curly snack,

00:19:17.556 --> 00:19:19.558
and they usually come flavored with cheese

00:19:19.558 --> 00:19:21.627
but are also available as salt and vinegar

00:19:21.627 --> 00:19:22.961
or as prawn cocktail versions.

00:19:22.961 --> 00:19:24.530
And then finally we have Squares.

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:26.598
Squares are these very thin,

00:19:26.598 --> 00:19:28.233
as you can imagine, square-shaped crisps.

00:19:28.233 --> 00:19:30.969
Very crunchy, usually quite
flavorful. I quite like those.

00:19:30.969 --> 00:19:32.638
And they come in salt and vinegar,

00:19:32.638 --> 00:19:34.706
cheese and onion, or ready salted.

00:19:34.706 --> 00:19:36.241
Lay's also makes dips.

00:19:36.241 --> 00:19:39.044
Creamy jalapeño, smooth ranch dip,

00:19:39.044 --> 00:19:40.913
and, of course, French onion.

00:19:40.913 --> 00:19:43.315
Yuelei says cheddar and sour cream.

00:19:45.584 --> 00:19:47.352
Yeah, that's really good.

00:19:47.352 --> 00:19:48.687
We also have a couple more crisp options

00:19:48.687 --> 00:19:50.255
sold under the Walkers
brand name in the UK

00:19:50.255 --> 00:19:51.890
which unfortunately we couldn't get today.

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:54.927
These include French
Fries, Bugles, and Mixups.

00:19:57.062 --> 00:19:58.363
Are there any questionable ingredients

00:19:58.363 --> 00:20:00.199
to look out for in your
Lay's and Walkers chips?

00:20:00.199 --> 00:20:02.034
As far as the basic salted version

00:20:02.034 --> 00:20:03.869
of Lay's chips go, we're fine.

00:20:03.869 --> 00:20:05.337
Both in the US and the UK,

00:20:05.337 --> 00:20:06.738
they are simply made up of

00:20:06.738 --> 00:20:09.208
potatoes, vegetable oil, and salt.

00:20:09.208 --> 00:20:10.509
But when you venture into other flavors,

00:20:10.509 --> 00:20:12.110
things can get a little more interesting.

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:13.145
For example, in the UK,

00:20:13.145 --> 00:20:15.447
several of our flavors
contain potassium chloride.

00:20:15.447 --> 00:20:17.182
In normal doses, this is a perfectly safe

00:20:17.182 --> 00:20:19.017
low-sodium alternative to salt.

00:20:19.017 --> 00:20:20.886
However, it's also one
of the three ingredients

00:20:20.886 --> 00:20:23.622
used in the three-drug
cocktail for lethal injections.

00:20:23.622 --> 00:20:25.057
Enough potassium chloride in your system

00:20:25.057 --> 00:20:27.492
will lead to an irregular
heartbeat and a cardiac arrest.

00:20:27.492 --> 00:20:29.361
We don't have that in our USA Lay's,

00:20:29.361 --> 00:20:31.630
but we do have caramel
color in our barbecue

00:20:31.630 --> 00:20:33.131
and honey barbecue chips.

00:20:33.131 --> 00:20:34.166
Ah, caramel color.

00:20:34.166 --> 00:20:36.368
It is a widely used food coloring,

00:20:36.368 --> 00:20:37.736
and it's also a controversial one.

00:20:37.736 --> 00:20:40.372
Certain types of caramel
color can contain a byproduct

00:20:40.372 --> 00:20:44.409
called 4-Me upper-case I. That's not an L.

00:20:44.409 --> 00:20:47.479
Studies show that it caused
cancer in rats and mice,

00:20:47.479 --> 00:20:49.181
leading to campaigns in support

00:20:49.181 --> 00:20:51.783
of banning it in foods. Makes sense.

00:20:51.783 --> 00:20:53.885
The FDA stopped short of banning it,

00:20:53.885 --> 00:20:57.489
claiming that humans don't come
close to levels of exposure

00:20:57.489 --> 00:20:59.625
that caused the rats' tumors.

00:20:59.625 --> 00:21:01.260
Sounds like a challenge.

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:03.028
But that didn't stop
the state of California

00:21:03.028 --> 00:21:05.697
adding it to its Proposition 65 list

00:21:05.697 --> 00:21:08.834
of chemicals, quote, "Known
to the state of California

00:21:08.834 --> 00:21:12.170
to cause cancer or reproductive
toxicity," end quote.

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:13.005
Another fun thing to note

00:21:13.005 --> 00:21:14.973
is that our smoky bacon
and roast chicken crisps

00:21:14.973 --> 00:21:16.975
are actually both
suitable for vegetarians.

00:21:16.975 --> 00:21:18.710
The flavoring is just
made up of other things

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.145
and doesn't include any meat extract.

00:21:21.913 --> 00:21:23.715
Which country has the
least healthy crisps?

00:21:23.715 --> 00:21:25.017
Let's compare the classic first.

00:21:25.017 --> 00:21:27.786
A 28-gram bag of classic Lay's in the US

00:21:27.786 --> 00:21:30.656
contains 160 calories.

00:21:30.656 --> 00:21:32.491
If we scale up the UK's 25-gram bag

00:21:32.491 --> 00:21:34.026
to account for that extra 3 grams,

00:21:34.026 --> 00:21:38.163
28 grams of UK ready salted
would contain 147 calories.

00:21:38.163 --> 00:21:41.667
So per gram, the UK's crisps
are healthier in every metric.

00:21:41.667 --> 00:21:42.734
OK, fine,

00:21:42.734 --> 00:21:45.003
but what about the least
healthy chip in each country?

00:21:45.003 --> 00:21:46.471
Over here, a lot of them are tied

00:21:46.471 --> 00:21:49.074
at 160 calories per 28-gram bag,

00:21:49.074 --> 00:21:52.344
but we did find that of
the 160-calorie chips,

00:21:52.344 --> 00:21:53.912
the highest fat content

00:21:53.912 --> 00:21:55.847
are in the cheddar and sour cream.

00:21:55.847 --> 00:21:57.182
Obviously the smaller bags.

00:21:57.182 --> 00:21:59.084
That makes them the least healthy.

00:21:59.084 --> 00:22:00.385
The least healthy crisps in the UK

00:22:00.385 --> 00:22:02.788
are the Strong hot
chicken wings Max crisps.

00:22:02.788 --> 00:22:05.123
28 grams of these would contain ...

00:22:05.123 --> 00:22:06.558
Honestly, my main
takeaway from this is that

00:22:06.558 --> 00:22:08.827
crisps might not be as unhealthy
as I thought they were.

00:22:08.827 --> 00:22:11.163
You could eat, like, 10 multipack
bags of the ready salted,

00:22:11.163 --> 00:22:12.931
and the only daily limit
you would have exceeded

00:22:12.931 --> 00:22:14.466
would be your fat intake.

00:22:14.466 --> 00:22:17.536
Yes, Harry, I believe that's
called death by deliciousness.

00:22:17.536 --> 00:22:18.570
I live by the motto,

00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:22.274
"Live fast, die fat, and
leave a salty corpse."

00:22:22.274 --> 00:22:23.742
That's actually my LinkedIn headline.

00:22:25.477 --> 00:22:27.045
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:22:27.045 --> 00:22:28.380
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:30.816
between Coca-Cola in the UK and the US.

00:22:30.816 --> 00:22:32.284
This is "Food Wars."

00:22:37.155 --> 00:22:39.624
In the UK, regular Coke
comes in eight portion sizes,

00:22:39.624 --> 00:22:42.427
starting with this mini can,
which is 150 milliliters.

00:22:42.427 --> 00:22:44.196
Then we have three
options which all include

00:22:44.196 --> 00:22:46.064
250 milliliters of Coke.

00:22:46.064 --> 00:22:48.633
Then we have our standard
can, which is 330 milliliters.

00:22:48.900 --> 00:22:51.536
Our standard plastic
bottle is 500 milliliters.

00:22:51.536 --> 00:22:53.805
From there, we move up to
this bottle, which is 1 liter.

00:22:53.805 --> 00:22:55.574
1.25 liters,

00:22:55.574 --> 00:22:57.175
1.5 liters,

00:22:57.175 --> 00:22:58.677
and 2.25 liters.

00:22:58.677 --> 00:23:00.178
It's worth noting that
these ones are only stocked

00:23:00.178 --> 00:23:02.714
by a limited number of
shops, including Iceland.

00:23:02.714 --> 00:23:04.282
The supermarket chain, not the country.

00:23:04.483 --> 00:23:07.552
And in the US, our classic
Coke comes in these sizes.

00:23:07.552 --> 00:23:10.088
The mini can, which is 7.5 ounces.

00:23:10.088 --> 00:23:12.624
Then this mini bottle, which is 8 ounces.

00:23:12.624 --> 00:23:14.793
Then we jump up to the
standard 12-ounce can.

00:23:14.793 --> 00:23:16.962
That also comes in a
little 12-ounce bottle.

00:23:16.962 --> 00:23:20.532
From there, we got this guy,
which is the 16.9 fluid ounces,

00:23:20.532 --> 00:23:22.901
aka 500 milliliters.

00:23:22.901 --> 00:23:24.970
Then we have a 20-ounce bottle.

00:23:24.970 --> 00:23:26.738
And finally, our biggest, the 2 liter,

00:23:28.673 --> 00:23:31.376
which is also 67.6 ounces.

00:23:31.376 --> 00:23:34.379
Now, that means as far as
Coca-Cola classic is concerned,

00:23:34.379 --> 00:23:38.316
the UK's largest size
is actually 12.5% larger

00:23:38.316 --> 00:23:39.317
than that in the US.

00:23:39.317 --> 00:23:41.319
There is a reason why we're
specifying regular Coke here.

00:23:41.319 --> 00:23:43.221
The UK government brought in a sugar tax,

00:23:43.221 --> 00:23:44.723
which raised the price of sugary drinks

00:23:44.723 --> 00:23:46.691
in an effort to reduce
people's sugar consumption.

00:23:46.691 --> 00:23:48.727
Instead of raising the prices
of some of their drinks,

00:23:48.727 --> 00:23:50.128
what Coca-Cola did was just to make

00:23:50.128 --> 00:23:52.264
the sugary versions of their
drinks a little bit smaller.

00:23:52.264 --> 00:23:54.566
For example, how the normal
largest size of regular Coke

00:23:54.566 --> 00:23:56.501
is 1.5 liters,

00:23:56.501 --> 00:23:59.304
whereas the largest size
of Coke Zero is 2 liters.

00:23:59.438 --> 00:24:02.007
Whereas here in the US, we
don't have a specific sugar tax.

00:24:02.007 --> 00:24:04.476
So we can get our bottles of
classic Coke and diet Coke

00:24:04.476 --> 00:24:06.178
in the same size and for the same price.

00:24:06.445 --> 00:24:08.046
As a consequence of the UK sugar rules,

00:24:08.046 --> 00:24:10.515
it actually means that
the 2.25 regular Coke

00:24:10.515 --> 00:24:12.284
isn't our largest bottle size.

00:24:12.284 --> 00:24:13.351
That crown

00:24:13.351 --> 00:24:14.252
[thud]

00:24:14.252 --> 00:24:15.387
goes to this,

00:24:15.387 --> 00:24:17.355
the 3-liter diet Coke bottle.

00:24:17.355 --> 00:24:19.658
Now, this absolute unit is 50% larger

00:24:19.658 --> 00:24:21.393
than the biggest bottle in America.

00:24:21.393 --> 00:24:23.261
If you're doing, like, a party, maybe?

00:24:23.261 --> 00:24:24.563
If you're buying that for yourself,

00:24:24.563 --> 00:24:26.731
like, you've got a problem.

00:24:26.731 --> 00:24:27.566
I'm sorry.

00:24:27.566 --> 00:24:31.102
That is ridiculously huge
and really hilarious.

00:24:31.102 --> 00:24:34.239
Now, I want to point
out that on Walmart.com,

00:24:34.239 --> 00:24:39.244
they have this 3-liter
bottle of diet Coke on it,

00:24:39.244 --> 00:24:41.213
but it's not available anywhere.

00:24:41.213 --> 00:24:44.416
So my assumption is at one
point in the United States,

00:24:44.416 --> 00:24:46.551
there was 3-liter bottles available.

00:24:46.551 --> 00:24:47.853
But if Walmart doesn't have it,

00:24:47.853 --> 00:24:49.254
I'm assuming it isn't anywhere.

00:24:49.254 --> 00:24:51.289
That being said, in terms
of multipack options,

00:24:51.289 --> 00:24:52.724
the US still comes out on top.

00:24:52.724 --> 00:24:55.360
Our single largest multipack

00:24:55.360 --> 00:24:58.997
is the 35-pack of 12-ounce cans.

00:24:58.997 --> 00:25:00.999
Let's get a picture of that on the screen.

00:25:00.999 --> 00:25:03.435
I ordered it online, and
here's what they sent me.

00:25:07.038 --> 00:25:10.775
24-pack, and nine loose cans.

00:25:10.775 --> 00:25:13.144
Now, correct me if I'm wrong,
but what's 24 plus nine?

00:25:13.144 --> 00:25:14.279
It ain't 35.

00:25:14.279 --> 00:25:16.414
And when I emailed the
place that I bought it from,

00:25:16.414 --> 00:25:18.750
they said, "Oh, sorry,
you're missing two cans,

00:25:18.750 --> 00:25:20.018
so we'll just refund you the two cans."

00:25:20.018 --> 00:25:22.053
And I'm like, "No, I
don't want the two cans,

00:25:22.053 --> 00:25:23.522
I want the 35-pack

00:25:23.522 --> 00:25:25.423
'cause that's what I'm
doing for this video,"

00:25:25.423 --> 00:25:27.526
and they just sent me $2
back, so thank you for that.

00:25:27.526 --> 00:25:30.495
Anyway, so then I go, nuts to this.

00:25:30.495 --> 00:25:32.297
I'm going to Walmart.com.

00:25:32.297 --> 00:25:34.199
Give me the 35-pack.

00:25:34.199 --> 00:25:35.233
Buy. Enter.

00:25:35.233 --> 00:25:37.168
And then they sent me

00:25:41.006 --> 00:25:44.309
three 12-packs, which
is more than 35 cans,

00:25:44.309 --> 00:25:45.744
so I guess technically
they're being generous,

00:25:45.744 --> 00:25:48.847
but once again, it's not
that I need 35 cans of soda.

00:25:48.847 --> 00:25:52.017
I need the 35-can pack for
this video specifically.

00:25:52.017 --> 00:25:55.453
There's a 35-can pack
somewhere in America,

00:25:55.453 --> 00:25:59.157
and everyone's just sending
me roughly 35 cans of soda.

00:25:59.157 --> 00:26:00.125
Thank you for that.

00:26:00.125 --> 00:26:02.193
Our largest single item is this.

00:26:05.964 --> 00:26:08.900
This is a 24-pack of 330-milliliter cans,

00:26:08.900 --> 00:26:11.536
which comes to a total of 7.92 liters.

00:26:14.873 --> 00:26:16.341
Here is everything that's in regular Coke.

00:26:16.341 --> 00:26:17.375
Harry: Carbonated water.
Joe: Carbonated water.

00:26:17.375 --> 00:26:18.310
Harry: Sugar.
Joe: High-fructose corn syrup.

00:26:18.310 --> 00:26:19.878
Harry: Color (caramel E150d).
Joe: Caramel color.

00:26:19.878 --> 00:26:20.879
Harry: Phosphoric acid.
Joe: Phosphoric acid.

00:26:20.879 --> 00:26:22.447
Harry: And natural flavorings,
Joe: And natural flavors.

00:26:22.447 --> 00:26:23.515
Harry: including caffeine.
Joe: Caffeine.

00:26:23.582 --> 00:26:25.283
Now, obviously we don't get
a full ingredients list,

00:26:25.283 --> 00:26:27.886
because the recipe of Coca-Cola
is a closely guarded secret.

00:26:27.886 --> 00:26:29.421
At the World of Coca-Cola in Atlanta,

00:26:29.421 --> 00:26:31.856
there's reportedly a vault which
contains the secret formula

00:26:31.856 --> 00:26:33.291
written down on a piece of paper.

00:26:33.291 --> 00:26:36.094
Who cares if the recipe gets loose?

00:26:36.094 --> 00:26:38.463
Coca-Cola, no one's gonna edge you up.

00:26:38.463 --> 00:26:39.898
Pepsi can't beat you.

00:26:39.898 --> 00:26:40.765
Who cares?

00:26:40.765 --> 00:26:42.233
I mean, how do you even make cola?

00:26:42.233 --> 00:26:43.435
You probably just go into the factory

00:26:43.435 --> 00:26:45.036
and eyeball it and figure it out.

00:26:45.036 --> 00:26:47.405
It's not super famous because
you don't know how to make it,

00:26:47.405 --> 00:26:50.342
it's super famous because
they edged everybody out.

00:26:50.342 --> 00:26:51.543
You won.

00:26:51.543 --> 00:26:52.377
Do you – I don't care.

00:26:52.377 --> 00:26:53.244
Do you want the recipe?

00:26:53.244 --> 00:26:53.912
I couldn't care less.

00:26:54.145 --> 00:26:55.647
So, what do we know about the recipe?

00:26:55.647 --> 00:26:56.815
Well, there is one obvious difference,

00:26:56.815 --> 00:26:59.584
and that's the use of
high-fructose corn syrup in the US

00:26:59.584 --> 00:27:01.486
versus the use of sugar in the UK.

00:27:01.653 --> 00:27:03.888
Corn syrup is everywhere in American food.

00:27:03.888 --> 00:27:05.957
It's cheaper for manufacturers to use

00:27:05.957 --> 00:27:08.126
because the government gives
subsidies to corn farmers,

00:27:08.126 --> 00:27:10.829
keeping the corn supply
high and the prices low.

00:27:10.829 --> 00:27:12.163
Should you be worried about consuming

00:27:12.163 --> 00:27:13.365
high-fructose corn syrup?

00:27:13.365 --> 00:27:14.799
The short answer is not really.

00:27:14.866 --> 00:27:16.001
Some studies have suggested

00:27:16.001 --> 00:27:17.102
that the negative effects of sugar

00:27:17.102 --> 00:27:19.437
tend to come from fructose
rather than from glucose,

00:27:19.437 --> 00:27:21.373
but the high fructose in
high-fructose corn syrup

00:27:21.373 --> 00:27:22.874
only relates to its fructose content

00:27:22.874 --> 00:27:24.542
in relation to other corn syrups.

00:27:24.542 --> 00:27:25.877
It actually still has less fructose

00:27:25.877 --> 00:27:27.479
than table sugar or than honey.

00:27:27.646 --> 00:27:30.015
The main difference it
causes might be the taste.

00:27:30.015 --> 00:27:32.050
You've heard Americans
talk about Mexican Coke.

00:27:32.050 --> 00:27:33.785
You can find it in most
Mexican restaurants

00:27:33.785 --> 00:27:34.919
and in some grocery stores

00:27:34.919 --> 00:27:37.155
next to the regular Coke
in the glass bottle.

00:27:37.155 --> 00:27:38.923
Mexican Coke is made with cane sugar;

00:27:38.923 --> 00:27:41.292
our regular Coke is made with
high-fructose corn syrup.

00:27:41.426 --> 00:27:43.795
People tend to like the Mexican Coke more

00:27:43.795 --> 00:27:45.630
because it has a sweeter sugary taste.

00:27:45.630 --> 00:27:49.734
So right now to compare and contrast,

00:27:49.734 --> 00:27:51.369
I'm going to do a blind taste test

00:27:51.369 --> 00:27:55.373
of both American Coke and Mexican Coke.

00:27:55.373 --> 00:27:56.541
