30 milliliters of
Tennessee whiskey we have,

00:37:34.018 --> 00:37:35.853
and then 20 milliliters of Disaronno.

00:37:37.021 --> 00:37:38.456
A delightful smoky Coke.

00:37:40.958 --> 00:37:42.293
Next we mix together.

00:37:44.362 --> 00:37:45.630
And there you have it. Thanks to Coke,

00:37:45.630 --> 00:37:48.499
we've put our own spin on a
Jack's godfather highball.

00:37:48.499 --> 00:37:49.333
Cheers.

00:37:50.968 --> 00:37:52.303
Ooh. That's delicious.

00:37:52.536 --> 00:37:56.073
Um, yeah, I'm not going
to make that drink,

00:37:56.073 --> 00:37:57.141
'cause I don't have all that stuff.

00:37:57.141 --> 00:37:59.477
So I'm going to go ahead
and make a Joe highball.

00:37:59.644 --> 00:38:02.413
First, get yourself the
biggest glass available.

00:38:02.413 --> 00:38:04.148
Step two: no ice.

00:38:04.148 --> 00:38:05.082
Find yourself some whiskey.

00:38:15.126 --> 00:38:15.760
Cheers, my man.

00:38:20.364 --> 00:38:21.465
Oh, man.

00:38:22.566 --> 00:38:23.501
What is in this?

00:38:23.501 --> 00:38:25.403
If I was to do it again,
I'd use less of this.

00:38:27.071 --> 00:38:28.072
It's iced tea, guys.

00:38:29.206 --> 00:38:30.408
I'm not gonna f---ing drink whiskey

00:38:30.408 --> 00:38:31.375
this early in the morning.

00:38:33.210 --> 00:38:34.011
You know what it tastes like?

00:38:34.278 --> 00:38:35.379
Flat Coke.

00:38:35.613 --> 00:38:36.681
Oh, man, I'm getting a headache though.

00:38:36.881 --> 00:38:39.750
Last but not least, in the
US, you have the option

00:38:39.750 --> 00:38:41.886
to order customized Coke bottles.

00:38:41.886 --> 00:38:43.521
Check out the one I made.

00:38:43.521 --> 00:38:45.356
Joe and Harry.

00:38:51.929 --> 00:38:53.764
Here's everything that's
in a 500-milliliter bottle

00:38:53.764 --> 00:38:55.766
of Coca-Cola in the UK.

00:38:55.766 --> 00:38:57.301
And here's everything in that same bottle

00:38:57.301 --> 00:38:58.736
of classic Coke in the US.

00:39:00.204 --> 00:39:01.305
That means that the UK's version

00:39:01.305 --> 00:39:03.374
actually has slightly more
calories in it than the US.

00:39:03.407 --> 00:39:04.675
Joe: And we have more sugar.

00:39:04.675 --> 00:39:07.144
And for some reason, our Coke
has a little bit of sodium,

00:39:07.144 --> 00:39:08.746
while the UK seems to have none.

00:39:08.879 --> 00:39:11.482
Obviously, the main thing to
look out for here is the sugar.

00:39:11.482 --> 00:39:13.751
500 milliliters in both the US and the UK

00:39:13.751 --> 00:39:15.986
contains over 100% of
your daily allowance.

00:39:15.986 --> 00:39:18.689
53 grams of sugar. [laughs]

00:39:18.689 --> 00:39:20.091
It does put it in perspective, doesn't it?

00:39:20.091 --> 00:39:21.525
You never see it laid out like that,

00:39:21.525 --> 00:39:22.960
but that is how much sugar is in Coke.

00:39:22.960 --> 00:39:24.595
And I drink a lot of Coke.

00:39:24.595 --> 00:39:25.062
That's concerning.

00:39:25.196 --> 00:39:27.431
It's also worth noting that both countries

00:39:27.431 --> 00:39:29.400
put the same amount of
caffeine in their Coke.

00:39:29.500 --> 00:39:31.268
For reference, the average
cup of filtered coffee

00:39:31.268 --> 00:39:33.270
contains about 96 milligrams of caffeine.

00:39:33.337 --> 00:39:35.606
So that's exactly double the
amount in this bottle of Coke.

00:39:35.673 --> 00:39:37.675
Interestingly, diet Coke is
actually more caffeinated

00:39:37.675 --> 00:39:38.542
than regular Coke.

00:39:38.576 --> 00:39:40.311
There's 63 milligrams in this bottle,

00:39:40.311 --> 00:39:41.579
which is a 30% increase.

00:39:41.712 --> 00:39:44.181
And it makes sense, 'cause
our Coke with coffee

00:39:44.181 --> 00:39:47.785
contains 69 milligrams of
caffeine per 12 fluid ounces.

00:39:47.785 --> 00:39:49.720
If you do the math to find
out the figure per ounce,

00:39:49.720 --> 00:39:51.322
it's double the caffeine
of a regular Coke.

00:39:51.322 --> 00:39:54.792
But the real caffeine king
is my boy Coke Energy.

00:39:57.061 --> 00:39:57.995
Mm.

00:39:58.963 --> 00:40:01.465
Whether you get the classic or the cherry,

00:40:01.465 --> 00:40:05.369
the 12-ounce can contains
114 milligrams of caffeine,

00:40:05.369 --> 00:40:07.371
which is triple the caffeine content

00:40:07.371 --> 00:40:09.640
of a regular Coke per ounce.

00:40:09.640 --> 00:40:11.942
Yo, don't I know it.

00:40:12.543 --> 00:40:13.978
From calorie count to portion sizes,

00:40:13.978 --> 00:40:15.446
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:40:15.446 --> 00:40:18.082
between Popeyes in the UK and the US.

00:40:18.082 --> 00:40:19.417
This is "Food Wars."

00:40:23.521 --> 00:40:26.190
The fountain drinks at
Popeyes come in three sizes.

00:40:26.190 --> 00:40:28.359
The small, which is 22 ounces,

00:40:28.359 --> 00:40:30.895
the medium, which is 30 ounces,

00:40:30.895 --> 00:40:35.733
and the large, which is,
of course, 40 ounces.

00:40:35.733 --> 00:40:37.501
40 ounces.

00:40:38.602 --> 00:40:40.004
That's so much soda.

00:40:40.004 --> 00:40:42.006
In the UK, drinks only come in two sizes,

00:40:42.006 --> 00:40:44.275
as a kids size or as a regular size.

00:40:44.275 --> 00:40:45.743
We're not sure how much
is in either of these,

00:40:45.743 --> 00:40:47.278
so we're going to measure them both.

00:40:47.278 --> 00:40:48.946
A little over 300.

00:40:54.251 --> 00:40:55.653
About 450.

00:40:59.924 --> 00:41:01.792
But those aren't the biggest, I say!

00:41:01.792 --> 00:41:03.194
Actually, at the Popeyes in the US,

00:41:03.194 --> 00:41:05.930
you can also get a gallon of sweet tea

00:41:06.797 --> 00:41:08.499
and unsweetened tea.

00:41:08.499 --> 00:41:12.269
One whole gallon.

00:41:12.269 --> 00:41:13.871
Ah, look at this!

00:41:13.871 --> 00:41:15.606
Gallon, gallon.

00:41:15.606 --> 00:41:17.942
Oh, and don't you hate
when dummies do that thing

00:41:17.942 --> 00:41:18.776
where they're like,

00:41:18.776 --> 00:41:21.879
"Hey, the medium is the
same size as the large!"

00:41:21.879 --> 00:41:23.848
And it never is, it's a total con, so.

00:41:23.848 --> 00:41:25.749
Medium soda, large cup.

00:41:29.687 --> 00:41:31.956
Oh, wow, guys!

00:41:31.956 --> 00:41:33.591
The medium's about the
same size as the large,

00:41:33.591 --> 00:41:35.826
except for, like, oh, I
don't know, 10 ounces!

00:41:35.826 --> 00:41:37.261
Dumb TikTokers. You guys aren't even ...

00:41:37.261 --> 00:41:39.129
out-of-your-league TikTokers.

00:41:39.129 --> 00:41:42.566
I'm the fast-food king online! All right?

00:41:46.003 --> 00:41:47.438
When was this cleaned last?

00:41:50.908 --> 00:41:54.612
Ooh,

00:41:54.612 --> 00:41:56.614
I'm gonna go 36. What do you think?

00:41:56.614 --> 00:41:58.682
I mean, it could have been
the amount to top of this cup,

00:41:58.682 --> 00:42:01.652
but again, you can't
fill this to the brim.

00:42:01.652 --> 00:42:02.887
You have to put a cap on it.

00:42:02.887 --> 00:42:05.289
In the UK, fries just
come as a regular serving.

00:42:05.289 --> 00:42:08.759
US, we got two Popeyes fries sizes,

00:42:08.759 --> 00:42:09.827
a regular and a large.

00:42:09.827 --> 00:42:11.562
The regular, as we have here,

00:42:11.562 --> 00:42:13.931
just came with the side of
the three-piece we got here,

00:42:13.931 --> 00:42:15.266
and of course a large,

00:42:15.266 --> 00:42:18.669
which is a box of just fries.

00:42:18.669 --> 00:42:19.637
Harry: We're going to weigh these to see

00:42:19.637 --> 00:42:21.205
how they compare to the US.

00:42:21.205 --> 00:42:22.773
Joe: We, of course, now are going to also

00:42:22.773 --> 00:42:25.342
weigh our largest fry.

00:42:26.443 --> 00:42:31.181
Do not sleep on these fries.

00:42:31.181 --> 00:42:32.683
You'll be surprised to learn

00:42:32.683 --> 00:42:36.153
that the inside of this
scale is disgusting.

00:42:36.153 --> 00:42:37.788
A Popeyes chicken sandwich in the UK

00:42:37.788 --> 00:42:41.692
weighs exactly 250 grams.

00:42:41.692 --> 00:42:43.827
Joe: In the US, it weighs

00:42:43.827 --> 00:42:47.398
270 grams.

00:42:47.398 --> 00:42:49.600
In the US, Popeyes signature chicken

00:42:49.600 --> 00:42:51.735
comes in seven serving sizes.

00:42:51.735 --> 00:42:52.670
We'll start with these.

00:42:52.670 --> 00:42:54.805
So, of course, the one-piece kids meal,

00:42:54.805 --> 00:42:58.642
then you can upgrade to
a two-piece regular meal,

00:42:58.642 --> 00:43:00.844
which comes with a side and a biscuit,

00:43:00.844 --> 00:43:02.947
or you can get yourself the three-piece,

00:43:02.947 --> 00:43:06.350
and a four-piece. Side and a biscuit.

00:43:06.350 --> 00:43:07.952
From there, you can get yourself

00:43:07.952 --> 00:43:10.020
an eight-piece family meal,

00:43:10.020 --> 00:43:12.957
the 12-piece for the family as well,

00:43:12.957 --> 00:43:14.992
or just for one person over a weekend,

00:43:14.992 --> 00:43:18.429
and the largest, the 16-piece.

00:43:18.429 --> 00:43:19.496
Are you kidding me?

00:43:19.496 --> 00:43:20.497
[laughs]

00:43:20.497 --> 00:43:23.634
How absurd is this? Look
at all this chicken.

00:43:23.634 --> 00:43:25.202
In the UK, the signature chicken comes

00:43:25.202 --> 00:43:26.537
as a two-piece meal,

00:43:26.537 --> 00:43:27.871
as a three-piece meal,

00:43:27.871 --> 00:43:29.306
as a six-piece sharer,

00:43:29.306 --> 00:43:30.574
as a nine-piece sharer,

00:43:30.574 --> 00:43:32.943
or our largest size, the 12-piece sharer.

00:43:32.943 --> 00:43:34.545
Let's weigh a wing, a thigh, and a leg

00:43:34.545 --> 00:43:36.180
to see whose chickens are bigger.

00:43:37.348 --> 00:43:39.583
So, in the UK, our thigh,
leg, and wing combo

00:43:39.583 --> 00:43:41.552
came to around 290 grams.

00:43:42.953 --> 00:43:46.256
Here we go. First guy up, the leg.

00:43:46.256 --> 00:43:49.093
Next up, got that wing.

00:43:49.093 --> 00:43:50.160
Kind of a wimpy-looking one.

00:43:50.160 --> 00:43:52.162
And this one, the thigh.

00:43:58.669 --> 00:43:59.903
How 'bout the tendies?

00:43:59.903 --> 00:44:02.272
In the US, we have these following sizes:

00:44:02.272 --> 00:44:03.941
A kids meal has a one-piece,

00:44:03.941 --> 00:44:07.311
but what's up? They gave us two!

00:44:07.311 --> 00:44:08.912
And then from there you get a three-piece,

00:44:08.912 --> 00:44:10.080
which they forgot,

00:44:11.181 --> 00:44:13.217
and then we have five-piece,

00:44:13.217 --> 00:44:14.351
comes with a side and a biscuit,

00:44:14.351 --> 00:44:15.285
eight pieces.

00:44:15.285 --> 00:44:17.621
I feel like they're getting
bigger as I go along.

00:44:17.621 --> 00:44:19.023
Look at the size of this tender.

00:44:19.023 --> 00:44:21.692
Then we have the 12-piece.

00:44:21.692 --> 00:44:23.327
I mean, guys, this is like a --

00:44:23.327 --> 00:44:24.328
look at this!

00:44:24.328 --> 00:44:25.729
Did you know they're this big?

00:44:25.729 --> 00:44:28.232
This is fantastic. I
love how big these are.

00:44:28.232 --> 00:44:30.467
That's what I'm talking
about, Popeyes! Thank you.

00:44:30.467 --> 00:44:33.103
And, of course, the 16-piece.

00:44:33.103 --> 00:44:34.438
Look at this bad boy.

00:44:34.438 --> 00:44:36.173
Look at the size of these guys.

00:44:36.173 --> 00:44:38.676
Tenders in the UK come
in four portion sizes,

00:44:38.676 --> 00:44:40.611
as a two-piece, which is the kids meal,

00:44:40.611 --> 00:44:44.815
as a three-piece, a
five-piece, and an eight-piece.

00:44:44.815 --> 00:44:46.183
Next up is the nuggets.

00:44:46.183 --> 00:44:47.951
These can be found in servings of

00:44:47.951 --> 00:44:49.553
a four-piece kids meal,

00:44:49.553 --> 00:44:51.188
a six-piece kids meal,

00:44:51.188 --> 00:44:52.322
eight-piece,

00:44:52.322 --> 00:44:53.957
the 12-piece,

00:44:53.957 --> 00:44:55.659
24-piece,

00:44:55.659 --> 00:44:57.261
36 pieces,

00:44:57.261 --> 00:45:00.097
and then this double pile right here,

00:45:00.097 --> 00:45:03.033
the biggest order, 48 pieces.

00:45:03.033 --> 00:45:05.836
And I have to say, does
not look like enough.

00:45:05.836 --> 00:45:09.773
I know I could destroy that
48-piece with confidence.

00:45:10.708 --> 00:45:11.542
What do we got here?

00:45:11.542 --> 00:45:13.811
Oh, look at this sticker! This is fun.

00:45:13.811 --> 00:45:15.245
Yeah, look at these guys!

00:45:15.245 --> 00:45:16.847
Look at this big one playing a saxophone,

00:45:16.847 --> 00:45:18.515
how fun is that?

00:45:18.515 --> 00:45:19.616
That's cool, right?

00:45:19.616 --> 00:45:21.351
In the UK, we actually
call our nuggets bites,

00:45:21.351 --> 00:45:22.853
and they come in the following sizes:

00:45:22.853 --> 00:45:24.488
There's a four-piece,
which is a kids meal,

00:45:24.488 --> 00:45:27.124
a six-piece, a nine-piece, and a 12-piece.

00:45:27.124 --> 00:45:28.726
Unfortunately, we
couldn't get these today.

00:45:28.726 --> 00:45:31.028
USA, we got biscuits, baby.

00:45:31.028 --> 00:45:33.197
These are the not-cookie biscuits

00:45:33.197 --> 00:45:35.232
that have come up before in
other "Food Wars" episodes.

00:45:35.232 --> 00:45:37.234
These are the biscuits biscuits,

00:45:37.234 --> 00:45:39.903
and at Popeyes, you can get them in one,

00:45:39.903 --> 00:45:42.473
either on its own or probably
with just about every meal.

00:45:42.473 --> 00:45:44.875
You can also get them in six.

00:45:44.875 --> 00:45:46.443
It's, like, rolling right down here.

00:45:46.443 --> 00:45:48.679
And you can also get them in 12.

00:45:48.679 --> 00:45:50.614
Just overflowing biscuits over here.

00:45:51.548 --> 00:45:53.717
We actually do have biscuits
on the UK Popeyes menu.

00:45:53.717 --> 00:45:56.153
If you order it as a
side, you get one biscuit.

00:45:56.153 --> 00:45:59.890
The biggest single item you
can get on the US Popeyes menu

00:45:59.890 --> 00:46:02.493
is this, the Bigger Family Feast.

00:46:02.493 --> 00:46:05.462
It comes with 12 pieces of chicken,

00:46:05.462 --> 00:46:06.830
five chicken sandwiches,

00:46:06.830 --> 00:46:10.567
two large sides, got the
slaw and the mashed potatoes,

00:46:10.567 --> 00:46:13.804
five biscuits, and five apple pies.

00:46:13.804 --> 00:46:16.673
This entire thing will set
you back about 60 bucks

00:46:16.673 --> 00:46:20.043
and clocks in at 10,000 calories

00:46:20.043 --> 00:46:22.346
if you choose a more calorific
side, like the fries.

00:46:22.346 --> 00:46:23.647
I did not.

00:46:23.647 --> 00:46:25.415
That pretty much dwarfs
our largest single item,

00:46:25.415 --> 00:46:27.117
which is this, the 12-piece sharer.

00:46:27.117 --> 00:46:29.686
You get 12 pieces of
chicken, four regular sides,

00:46:29.686 --> 00:46:31.455
four biscuits, and four drinks,

00:46:31.455 --> 00:46:33.957
all for the price of
24 pounds and 95 pence,

00:46:33.957 --> 00:46:37.060
which was around $33.50
at the time of recording.

00:46:39.930 --> 00:46:40.864
Mm.

00:46:40.864 --> 00:46:42.499
We're so bad at fried chicken in the UK.

00:46:42.499 --> 00:46:44.168
We just don't do it well.

00:46:44.168 --> 00:46:46.770
But this, I gotta say,

00:46:46.770 --> 00:46:49.306
I feel like a certain Kentucky-based chain

00:46:49.306 --> 00:46:50.641
has had the monopoly for far too long,

00:46:50.641 --> 00:46:51.642
and they've let their standards slip.

00:46:51.642 --> 00:46:53.143
So this is really good.

00:46:53.143 --> 00:46:54.178
I'm thrilled that the standards

00:46:54.178 --> 00:46:55.879
are hopefully going to get raised.

00:47:00.050 --> 00:47:02.386
And here's everything you
can find at a US Popeyes

00:47:02.386 --> 00:47:04.655
you won't find in the UK.

00:47:04.655 --> 00:47:05.956
And here are most of
the things you'll find

00:47:05.956 --> 00:47:08.258
at a UK Popeyes that you
won't find in the US.

00:47:08.258 --> 00:47:09.126
Let's start with the chicken.

00:47:09.126 --> 00:47:11.829
There are two main exclusive
chicken options in the UK.

00:47:11.829 --> 00:47:15.065
Firstly in the UK, we can get
a chicken sandwich deluxe.

00:47:15.065 --> 00:47:16.333
It's just a Popeyes chicken sandwich,

00:47:16.333 --> 00:47:18.669
but there's cheese and
lettuce on here as well.

00:47:20.637 --> 00:47:21.471
What he means to say

00:47:21.471 --> 00:47:22.973
is they took a delicious chicken sandwich

00:47:22.973 --> 00:47:25.175
and added a bunch of junk.

00:47:25.175 --> 00:47:27.678
Deluxe means vegetables,

00:47:27.678 --> 00:47:31.448
aka the junk I don't want on
my crispy chicken sandwich.

00:47:31.448 --> 00:47:33.350
Popeyes in the UK also sell hot wings.

00:47:33.350 --> 00:47:38.021
These come in orders of
three, five, eight, 12, or 20.

00:47:38.021 --> 00:47:39.323
Now, it might surprise
some American viewers,

00:47:39.323 --> 00:47:40.290
but London in particular

00:47:40.290 --> 00:47:41.792
has a pretty big chicken-shop culture,

00:47:41.792 --> 00:47:43.527
and we're pretty passionate
about our hot wings,

00:47:43.527 --> 00:47:45.162
so let's see how these measure up.

00:47:45.162 --> 00:47:46.563
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:47:46.563 --> 00:47:49.967
Don't get it twisted.
We're the wings country,

00:47:49.967 --> 00:47:51.068
and we should have those.

00:47:51.068 --> 00:47:53.003
I have no idea why we don't have those.

00:47:56.640 --> 00:47:58.308
That to me is a very good chicken wing.

00:47:58.308 --> 00:48:00.344
Good level of heat, very
crispy on the outside,

00:48:00.344 --> 00:48:02.713
very juicy on the inside,
what more can you want?

00:48:02.713 --> 00:48:05.515
We only have one exclusive chicken item.

00:48:05.515 --> 00:48:06.516
Well, it's technically not an item,

00:48:06.516 --> 00:48:07.985
it's more of a style of chicken.

00:48:07.985 --> 00:48:09.052
Both in the US and the UK,

00:48:09.052 --> 00:48:10.754
they have the spicy and
they have the regular,

00:48:10.754 --> 00:48:13.690
but we also have something
called the blackened chicken.

00:48:13.690 --> 00:48:16.059
It is a chicken option without breading,

00:48:16.059 --> 00:48:17.761
therefore, who cares?

00:48:17.761 --> 00:48:19.997
And it comes in the form
of sandwich or tenders.

00:48:19.997 --> 00:48:22.432
Here it is, blackened chicken.

00:48:22.432 --> 00:48:24.635
It's called fried chicken for a reason.

00:48:24.635 --> 00:48:27.070
This is just, like, cooked on a grill?

00:48:27.070 --> 00:48:29.506
Grilled chicken at Popeyes.

00:48:29.506 --> 00:48:31.174
What is wrong with you?

00:48:33.176 --> 00:48:34.478
Oh.

00:48:34.478 --> 00:48:35.545
Nope.

00:48:35.545 --> 00:48:36.580
In both the UK and the US,

00:48:36.580 --> 00:48:37.814
Popeyes chicken sandwiches,

00:48:37.814 --> 00:48:39.316
fried chicken, and chicken tenders

00:48:39.316 --> 00:48:41.385
are available as either classic or spicy.

00:48:41.385 --> 00:48:43.453
One interesting fact is that
someone from Popeyes told us

00:48:43.453 --> 00:48:45.656
that the UK version of the spicy chicken

00:48:45.656 --> 00:48:47.691
is actually hotter than it is in America,

00:48:47.691 --> 00:48:49.259
after they tried it on some focus groups

00:48:49.259 --> 00:48:51.395
and they kept asking them
to crank up the heat.

00:48:51.395 --> 00:48:53.697
Who said British people
can't handle spices, huh?

00:48:57.834 --> 00:48:58.902
Now, this is not an exclusive

00:48:58.902 --> 00:49:00.203
because it's available in both countries.

00:49:00.203 --> 00:49:01.605
However, this is my first time

00:49:01.605 --> 00:49:03.740
trying an American-style biscuit.

00:49:03.740 --> 00:49:05.008
Now, the obvious statement is that, to me,

00:49:05.008 --> 00:49:06.710
this just looks like a scone.

00:49:06.710 --> 00:49:08.645
The color is there, the shape is there,

00:49:08.645 --> 00:49:10.881
the kind of flaky layers are there.

00:49:10.881 --> 00:49:12.115
It even kind of smells like a scone.

00:49:12.115 --> 00:49:13.984
And the fact that this is
being served with fried chicken

00:49:13.984 --> 00:49:16.687
to me and to I think most
British people is really weird.

00:49:20.023 --> 00:49:21.792
Don't get me wrong, this is tasty,

00:49:21.792 --> 00:49:23.460
I'm just still struggling
to see any differences

00:49:23.460 --> 00:49:25.329
between this and a British scone.

00:49:25.329 --> 00:49:27.464
Popeyes in the US doesn't
just serve chicken,

00:49:27.464 --> 00:49:29.366
it also has seafood,

00:49:29.366 --> 00:49:31.168
something you can't
find in the UK Popeyes.

00:49:31.168 --> 00:49:33.437
Now, the US Popeyes did for a while

00:49:33.437 --> 00:49:35.105
have a Cajun flounder sandwich,

00:49:35.105 --> 00:49:37.808
which is a fried flounder fillet in a bun

00:49:37.808 --> 00:49:39.643
with some pickles and tartar sauce.

00:49:39.643 --> 00:49:41.845
At the recording of this,
it is no longer available.

00:49:41.845 --> 00:49:43.113
I don't know if it was
a limited-time thing

00:49:43.113 --> 00:49:45.215
or they just stopped, they're
taking a break, I don't know.

00:49:45.215 --> 00:49:46.984
But you can still get the popcorn shrimp.

00:49:46.984 --> 00:49:48.051
This is it.

00:49:48.051 --> 00:49:52.389
And it comes in a quarter-pound serving.

00:49:52.389 --> 00:49:53.757
There are no seafood options in the UK,

00:49:53.757 --> 00:49:55.058
but we do have one vegan option

00:49:55.058 --> 00:49:56.226
which you guys don't have in the US,

00:49:56.226 --> 00:49:58.028
and that's the Creole red bean sandwich.

00:49:58.028 --> 00:50:00.130
This is a 100% plant-based red bean patty

00:50:00.130 --> 00:50:02.332
with some tomato, some
lettuce, and a Creole sauce,

00:50:02.332 --> 00:50:04.368
but unfortunately we weren't
able to get one today.

00:50:04.368 --> 00:50:05.669
I will say the Popeyes menu in the US

00:50:05.669 --> 00:50:07.304
doesn't look very vegetarian-friendly,

00:50:07.304 --> 00:50:08.705
so maybe if this takes off in the UK,

00:50:08.705 --> 00:50:10.007
you guys can get it too.

00:50:10.007 --> 00:50:11.308
Whatever the hell that thing is,

00:50:11.308 --> 00:50:14.845
100% plant-based red bean pat -- ugh.

00:50:14.845 --> 00:50:16.980
That will never touch American shores.

00:50:17.814 --> 00:50:19.750
That can stay in the UK.

00:50:19.750 --> 00:50:23.086
No one's going to Popeyes for
vegetarian, vegan anything.

00:50:23.086 --> 00:50:25.288
It's a fried-chicken place. So no.

00:50:25.288 --> 00:50:27.724
Now, we have two sides that
are exclusive to the US.

00:50:27.724 --> 00:50:29.226
Red beans and rice.

00:50:29.226 --> 00:50:30.127
Grr!

00:50:30.127 --> 00:50:33.563
Oh, do we got a bad boy? A thingy-thing?

00:50:33.563 --> 00:50:36.166
Did they not give us any silverware?

00:50:36.166 --> 00:50:39.436
Mystery spoon from somewhere
in the office, all right.

00:50:39.436 --> 00:50:42.172
Red beans and rice, there it is.

00:50:42.172 --> 00:50:44.641
And coleslaw.

00:50:44.641 --> 00:50:46.343
We just have the one
exclusive side in the UK,

00:50:46.343 --> 00:50:47.210
and it's onion rings.

00:50:47.210 --> 00:50:48.445
These are battered using buttermilk,

00:50:48.445 --> 00:50:49.746
similarly to the chicken.

00:50:49.746 --> 00:50:51.982
Unfortunately, we weren't able
to get these today either.

00:50:51.982 --> 00:50:53.784
I got a bunch of sauces in front of me,

00:50:53.784 --> 00:50:56.153
and you know what that means! It's:

00:50:56.153 --> 00:50:57.788
Sauce Talk.

00:50:57.788 --> 00:51:00.690
We've got a tartar sauce.

00:51:00.690 --> 00:51:03.560
The Creole cocktail sauce.

00:51:03.560 --> 00:51:07.664
Creole is a type of cuisine in Louisiana.

00:51:07.664 --> 00:51:09.766
Blackened ranch.

00:51:09.766 --> 00:51:11.134
Was this supposed to be
for the blackened chicken,

00:51:11.134 --> 00:51:12.002
do you think?

00:51:12.002 --> 00:51:14.805
And of course we have
regular buttermilk ranch.

00:51:14.805 --> 00:51:16.606
Well, we already know what ranch is.

00:51:18.241 --> 00:51:19.242
Ranchy.

00:51:19.242 --> 00:51:20.477
Blackened ranch.

00:51:22.746 --> 00:51:24.214
Oh, that's way better.

00:51:24.214 --> 00:51:25.916
The sweet heat.

00:51:25.916 --> 00:51:27.317
Had this earlier with the tenders,

00:51:27.317 --> 00:51:29.352
can confirm, fantastic sauce.

00:51:29.352 --> 00:51:31.488
Wild honey mustard

00:51:31.488 --> 00:51:34.724
and the bayou Buffalo sauce.

00:51:34.724 --> 00:51:37.360
In the UK, we have the
following exclusive sauces:

00:51:37.360 --> 00:51:39.563
we have this voodoo sweet chili sauce,

00:51:39.563 --> 00:51:42.466
which could be quite similar
to the US's sweet heat sauce.

00:51:42.466 --> 00:51:44.301
Then we have a garlic mayo

00:51:44.301 --> 00:51:46.002
as well as a mango habanero sauce,

00:51:46.002 --> 00:51:47.170
which sounds really good.

00:51:47.170 --> 00:51:48.004
It's not an exclusive,

00:51:48.004 --> 00:51:49.406
but shout-out to the Mardi Gras mustard,

00:51:49.406 --> 00:51:51.174
because this stuff slaps.

00:51:54.411 --> 00:51:55.679
Now, it's not exactly an exclusive,

00:51:55.679 --> 00:51:56.646
but it's worth a shout-out.

00:51:56.646 --> 00:51:59.082
Musician Megan Thee Stallion

00:51:59.082 --> 00:52:01.051
recently launched a collab with Popeyes

00:52:01.051 --> 00:52:02.586
and released the Hottie Sauce.

00:52:02.586 --> 00:52:04.121
You can get it as a side for dip

00:52:04.121 --> 00:52:05.622
or pre-add it to your chicken sandwich.

00:52:05.622 --> 00:52:06.456
Or if you're in the UK,

00:52:06.456 --> 00:52:08.225
you can dip a hot wing
into the Hottie Sauce

00:52:08.225 --> 00:52:09.392
and have a hot wing summer.

00:52:10.260 --> 00:52:12.629
She's also becoming a Popeyes franchisee,

00:52:12.629 --> 00:52:15.198
as she is opening her own Popeyes soon.

00:52:15.198 --> 00:52:17.100
And then underneath this, it says,

00:52:17.100 --> 00:52:20.704
"Need some 'WAP' content
here, open to ideas."

00:52:20.704 --> 00:52:23.140
I'm assuming she is the
one who did the song "WAP"?

00:52:23.140 --> 00:52:24.207
I don't know who this person is.

00:52:24.207 --> 00:52:26.009
I've never heard "WAP."

00:52:26.009 --> 00:52:28.078
I just know it as a
reference on the internet.

00:52:29.779 --> 00:52:32.616
And I am going to bask in the glory

00:52:32.616 --> 00:52:34.050
that only some my age can,

00:52:34.050 --> 00:52:37.354
of not having any idea
what a popular thing is.

00:52:37.354 --> 00:52:38.455
Ah.

00:52:38.455 --> 00:52:39.689
Desserts!

00:52:39.689 --> 00:52:43.160
This is a cinnamon apple pie.

00:52:46.963 --> 00:52:49.266
Oh, my God [mumbles].

00:52:49.266 --> 00:52:50.066
What?

00:52:50.066 --> 00:52:51.201
And ...

00:52:51.201 --> 00:52:52.035
ugh!

00:52:54.137 --> 00:52:56.406
Chocolate chip cookies.

00:52:56.406 --> 00:52:58.241
Was she with Paul Davis,

00:52:58.241 --> 00:52:59.910
Pete Davidson for
awhile? Was that the one?

00:53:01.344 --> 00:53:02.979
We have an exclusive
dessert option of our own,

00:53:02.979 --> 00:53:04.247
which is ice cream sundaes.

00:53:04.247 --> 00:53:06.449
Now, these are available
in the following flavors:

00:53:06.449 --> 00:53:09.719
vanilla, chocolate, caramel,

00:53:09.719 --> 00:53:12.122
with Oreos, or with Lotus Biscoff.

00:53:12.122 --> 00:53:13.490
You can also pay an extra 50 pence

00:53:13.490 --> 00:53:15.192
to add little pieces of Oreo or Biscoff

00:53:15.192 --> 00:53:16.359
to any of these sundaes.

00:53:16.359 --> 00:53:17.494
If you've watched "Food
Wars" for long enough,

00:53:17.494 --> 00:53:19.362
you'll know that I really
don't like Biscoff,

00:53:19.362 --> 00:53:20.897
and I know that's a very
controversial opinion,

00:53:20.897 --> 00:53:22.899
so don't send for me, please.

00:53:22.899 --> 00:53:24.968
All right, so before you saw
those big gallons of tea.

00:53:24.968 --> 00:53:28.004
There was sweet tea and
unsweetened tea. Very nice.

00:53:28.004 --> 00:53:30.640
We also have a premium lemonade.
That's this right here.

00:53:30.640 --> 00:53:33.210
I've been sipping on because
this chicken is getting to me.

00:53:34.144 --> 00:53:36.313
They also have premium
strawberry lemonade,

00:53:36.313 --> 00:53:39.883
and they also have this
right here, Hawaiian Punch.

00:53:39.883 --> 00:53:41.384
You guys don't know
what Hawaiian Punch is?

00:53:41.384 --> 00:53:43.486
It is fruit punch.

00:53:45.956 --> 00:53:48.391
Oh, yeah, all the good
stuff's at the bottom.

00:53:48.391 --> 00:53:51.494
And ginger ale. Ugh, I have
a headache all of a sudden.

00:53:51.494 --> 00:53:53.096
We have a range of
exclusive drinks in the UK,

00:53:53.096 --> 00:53:54.798
some of which are hot and
some of which are cold.

00:53:54.798 --> 00:53:55.799
We'll start with the hot drinks.

00:53:55.799 --> 00:53:57.167
It wouldn't be a British fast-food menu

00:53:57.167 --> 00:53:58.635
unless you could get a cup of tea.

00:53:58.635 --> 00:53:59.936
Then we have a range of hot coffees,

00:53:59.936 --> 00:54:02.606
including a cappuccino, an Americano,

00:54:02.606 --> 00:54:04.174
a flat white, and a latte.

00:54:04.174 --> 00:54:05.075
Then we're on to the cold drinks,

00:54:05.075 --> 00:54:06.176
including some bottled options,

00:54:06.176 --> 00:54:07.711
like this Oasis summer fruits,

00:54:07.711 --> 00:54:10.914
this sparkling water, and
this orange Capri Sun.

00:54:10.914 --> 00:54:11.948
Of all the linguistic differences

00:54:11.948 --> 00:54:12.983
between the States and the UK,

00:54:12.983 --> 00:54:14.551
this might be the one
that annoys me the most.

00:54:14.551 --> 00:54:17.587
We pronounce this CAP-ri Sun.
You pronounce it Cap-RI Sun.

00:54:17.587 --> 00:54:18.421
You're putting the emphasis

00:54:18.421 --> 00:54:20.924
on the completely wrong part
of the word. Get it right.

00:54:20.924 --> 00:54:22.092
In the UK, you can also get a range

00:54:22.092 --> 00:54:23.226
of hand-spun milkshakes,

00:54:23.226 --> 00:54:24.928
which unfortunately we couldn't get today.

00:54:24.928 --> 00:54:25.762
When they are available,

00:54:25.762 --> 00:54:27.464
you can get them in similar
flavors to the sundaes.

00:54:27.464 --> 00:54:30.834
They come as Biscoff,
Oreo, vanilla, chocolate,

00:54:30.834 --> 00:54:32.435
caramel, or also strawberry.

00:54:32.435 --> 00:54:33.270
And just like the sundaes,

00:54:33.270 --> 00:54:34.504
you can pay an additional 50 pence

00:54:34.504 --> 00:54:36.640
for an additional Biscoff or Oreo topping.

00:54:39.409 --> 00:54:40.977
The chicken sandwich from a UK Popeyes

00:54:40.977 --> 00:54:42.112
contains the following.

00:54:43.413 --> 00:54:45.448
If you get the chicken
sandwich at a US Popeyes,

00:54:45.448 --> 00:54:47.450
it contains this.

00:54:47.450 --> 00:54:48.385
What if you made it a meal?

00:54:48.385 --> 00:54:51.521
You add the regular serving
of Popeyes Cajun fries,

00:54:51.521 --> 00:54:53.556
you'll be adding the following.

00:54:53.556 --> 00:54:55.925
A side of fries in the UK
contains the following.

00:54:58.094 --> 00:54:59.396
Poof!

00:54:59.396 --> 00:55:01.131
Add this medium Coke to the mix,

00:55:01.131 --> 00:55:03.433
and you're adding 368 calories,

00:55:03.433 --> 00:55:05.769
99 carbs, all of those are sugar,

00:55:05.769 --> 00:55:07.937
and 88 milligrams of sodium.

00:55:07.937 --> 00:55:11.241
And a regular Coke in
the UK adds 180 calories,

00:55:11.241 --> 00:55:13.343
zero grams of fat or saturated fat,

00:55:13.343 --> 00:55:16.079
45.6 grams of carbs,
all of which are sugars,

00:55:16.079 --> 00:55:17.380
and zero sodium.

00:55:17.380 --> 00:55:19.316
And what is the total of this US meal?

00:55:19.316 --> 00:55:22.686
1,335 calories,

00:55:22.686 --> 00:55:24.621
56 grams of total fat,

00:55:24.621 --> 00:55:26.956
19 of those grams are saturated fat,

00:55:26.956 --> 00:55:29.259
182 grams of carbs,

00:55:29.259 --> 00:55:31.995
106.5 of those grams of sugar,

00:55:31.995 --> 00:55:35.765
and 2,118 milligrams of sodium.

00:55:35.765 --> 00:55:37.467
Yo.

00:55:37.467 --> 00:55:38.635
The UK total:

00:55:38.635 --> 00:55:40.003
1,300 calories,

00:55:40.003 --> 00:55:41.538
63.7 grams of fat,

00:55:41.538 --> 00:55:43.673
of which 20.4 grams of saturated,

00:55:43.673 --> 00:55:45.742
135.4 grams of carbs,

00:55:45.742 --> 00:55:47.877
of which 54.8 grams are sugars,

00:55:47.877 --> 00:55:50.547
and 1,160 milligrams of sodium.

00:55:50.547 --> 00:55:52.549
Obviously the sugar stats here look bad,

00:55:52.549 --> 00:55:53.817
but in Popeyes' defense,

00:55:53.817 --> 00:55:55.785
a majority of the sugar is coming from

00:55:55.785 --> 00:55:58.088
this 30 ounces -- [chuckles] 30 ounces --

00:55:58.088 --> 00:55:59.055
of Coca-Cola.

00:55:59.055 --> 00:56:00.957
Now, if you got a sugar-free soda instead,

00:56:00.957 --> 00:56:02.392
it would be a much lower figure.

00:56:02.392 --> 00:56:04.194
The meal does contain, however,

00:56:04.194 --> 00:56:07.097
95% of your daily saturated fat

00:56:07.097 --> 00:56:10.400
as well as 92% of your daily sodium.

00:56:10.400 --> 00:56:11.835
Perhaps surprisingly, it seems as if

00:56:11.835 --> 00:56:13.536
the fat and saturated fat totals

00:56:13.536 --> 00:56:15.839
are actually higher in the
UK than they are in the US.

00:56:15.839 --> 00:56:17.674
This meal would take you just over 100%

00:56:17.674 --> 00:56:19.809
of your daily saturated fat allowance.

00:56:19.809 --> 00:56:22.579
However, the sodium
content is way higher here

00:56:22.579 --> 00:56:23.747
than it is in the UK.

00:56:23.747 --> 00:56:25.648
The biggest difference comes
in the chicken sandwich.

00:56:25.648 --> 00:56:27.951
This guy right here, for some reason,

00:56:27.951 --> 00:56:32.756
has 260% more sodium than that in the UK.

00:56:36.025 --> 00:56:38.161
Unfortunately, Popeyes has not disclosed

00:56:38.161 --> 00:56:41.331
a full ingredients list
in the US, only allergens.

00:56:41.331 --> 00:56:42.632
It's a similar deal in the UK.

00:56:42.632 --> 00:56:44.501
Popeyes doesn't disclose
a full ingredients list,

00:56:44.501 --> 00:56:45.468
just allergens.

00:56:45.468 --> 00:56:47.670
The only sort of surprising
thing we found out in the US

00:56:47.670 --> 00:56:50.573
is that there is fish present
in the beans and rice.

00:56:50.573 --> 00:56:53.343
But what else do we know
about the Popeyes food?

00:56:53.343 --> 00:56:54.177
Ah!

00:56:54.177 --> 00:56:55.745
Well, for one, on the website,

00:56:55.745 --> 00:56:58.281
there is a list of a
slightly vague commitment

00:56:58.281 --> 00:57:00.750
to removing all artificial
colors, flavors,

00:57:00.750 --> 00:57:02.452
and preservatives from their fried chicken

00:57:02.452 --> 00:57:04.287
by the end of 2022.

00:57:04.287 --> 00:57:06.689
So, that's this year,
guys. Better get on it.

00:57:06.689 --> 00:57:07.791
Also by the end of this year,

00:57:07.791 --> 00:57:11.161
they want to remove all
MSG from their chicken.

00:57:11.161 --> 00:57:12.662
Now, correct me if I'm wrong,

00:57:12.662 --> 00:57:13.863
but that implies they currently

00:57:13.863 --> 00:57:15.965
are using MSG on the chicken.

00:57:15.965 --> 00:57:18.234
But how much and to which chicken dishes

00:57:18.234 --> 00:57:19.702
they're actually adding MSG,

00:57:19.702 --> 00:57:21.371
they have not specified.

00:57:21.371 --> 00:57:23.473
They also want to use only cage-free eggs

00:57:23.473 --> 00:57:26.042
by the end of 2025.

00:57:26.042 --> 00:57:28.011
Take your time there, guys, jeez.

00:57:28.011 --> 00:57:30.513
Also, cage-free "eggs"?

00:57:30.513 --> 00:57:32.115
What about the chickens?

00:57:32.115 --> 00:57:33.550
One interesting thing is that in the UK,

00:57:33.550 --> 00:57:35.351
Popeyes has pledged to
make all its chicken halal,

00:57:35.351 --> 00:57:37.253
meaning it's suitable
for Muslim people to eat.

00:57:37.253 --> 00:57:39.923
Popeyes UK also uses Red
Tractor-assured chicken.

00:57:39.923 --> 00:57:41.224
This is a farming standards board

00:57:41.224 --> 00:57:43.426
which oversees poultry farming in the UK.

00:57:43.426 --> 00:57:44.461
To be Red Tractor-assured,

00:57:44.461 --> 00:57:46.563
you can't do things like
wash your chicken in chlorine

00:57:46.563 --> 00:57:48.131
or use antibiotics on your chicken,

00:57:48.131 --> 00:57:51.067
unless it's approved by a vet
to treat a specific illness.

00:57:51.067 --> 00:57:53.203
Red Tractor doesn't exist in the US,

00:57:53.203 --> 00:57:55.305
but Popeyes does say it uses chicken

00:57:55.305 --> 00:57:58.141
free from added hormones and steroids.

00:57:58.141 --> 00:57:59.943
There's a commitment on Popeyes' website

00:57:59.943 --> 00:58:02.212
to removing antibiotics from its chickens

00:58:02.212 --> 00:58:03.613
by the end of 2021.

00:58:03.613 --> 00:58:04.681
So that's right around the corner

00:58:04.681 --> 00:58:05.748
at the time of recording this,

00:58:05.748 --> 00:58:08.218
and we reached out to them
for what was going on,

00:58:08.218 --> 00:58:10.753
and they told us X, [laughs]

00:58:10.753 --> 00:58:13.089
which is code for nothing.

00:58:13.089 --> 00:58:14.757
Red Tractor certification also means

00:58:14.757 --> 00:58:16.860
that chickens must be kept
in a safe, comfortable,

00:58:16.860 --> 00:58:18.995
hygienic, and sufficiently sized housing;

00:58:18.995 --> 00:58:20.697
given a full, healthy diet;

00:58:20.697 --> 00:58:23.132
and have permanent access
to environmental enrichment

00:58:23.132 --> 00:58:24.701
that is suitable for their needs.

00:58:24.701 --> 00:58:26.669
Again, we do not have
Red Tractor in the US,

00:58:26.669 --> 00:58:28.771
but Popeyes claims it wants to, quote,

00:58:28.771 --> 00:58:30.907
"promote practices that support

00:58:30.907 --> 00:58:33.109
and address the globally recognized

00:58:33.109 --> 00:58:36.246
five freedoms of animal
welfare," end quote.

00:58:36.246 --> 00:58:38.314
These principles broadly line up

00:58:38.314 --> 00:58:41.284
with the Red Tractor
guarantees, which are:

00:58:41.284 --> 00:58:42.952
freedom from hunger and thirst,

00:58:42.952 --> 00:58:44.554
freedom from discomfort,

00:58:44.554 --> 00:58:46.456
freedom from pain, injury, and disease,

00:58:46.456 --> 00:58:48.791
freedom to express
normal, natural behaviors,

00:58:48.791 --> 00:58:51.594
like accommodating for
chickens' instinct to roost,

00:58:51.594 --> 00:58:54.230
and freedom from fear and distress.

00:58:54.230 --> 00:58:56.299
I don't even get those freedoms!

00:58:56.299 --> 00:58:57.433
I'm terrified all the time!

00:58:57.433 --> 00:58:58.268
[chicken clucks]

00:58:58.268 --> 00:59:00.970
So it looks like they're aiming
for equivalent standards,

00:59:00.970 --> 00:59:04.073
even if they don't have
a nice Red Tractor badge

00:59:04.073 --> 00:59:06.309
or whatever to prove
that they've achieved it.

00:59:06.309 --> 00:59:08.845
Now, obviously Popeyes is a
Louisiana fast-food chain.

00:59:08.845 --> 00:59:10.780
Joe asked me to try and
find Louisiana on a map.

00:59:10.780 --> 00:59:12.248
I don't know much about
American geography.

00:59:12.248 --> 00:59:14.784
I can tell you where California is,

00:59:14.784 --> 00:59:17.820
where Texas is, where Florida is.

00:59:17.820 --> 00:59:19.923
New York is somewhere over here, I think.

00:59:20.924 --> 00:59:23.860
If I had to hazard a guess
as to where Louisiana was,

00:59:23.860 --> 00:59:25.295
I mean, it's the South, right?

00:59:25.295 --> 00:59:26.296
It's the South.

00:59:26.296 --> 00:59:27.397
Maybe ...

00:59:28.665 --> 00:59:30.800
is it, like, this one?

00:59:30.800 --> 00:59:32.268
Maybe that one there.

00:59:32.735 --> 00:59:34.370
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:59:34.370 --> 00:59:35.805
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:59:35.805 --> 00:59:38.274
between M&amp;M's in the UK and the US.

00:59:38.274 --> 00:59:39.375
This is "Food Wars."

00:59:41.945 --> 00:59:43.680
Here in the US, we have eight

00:59:43.680 --> 00:59:46.215
different portion sizes of M&amp;M's.

00:59:46.215 --> 00:59:47.116
All the way at the end here,

00:59:47.116 --> 00:59:49.686
the smallest portion is
known as the fun size.

00:59:49.686 --> 00:59:53.122
This little guy is 0.6
ounces, or 18 grams.

00:59:53.122 --> 00:59:56.292
Then, single size bag, 1.69 ounces.

00:59:56.292 --> 00:59:57.860
Then we go up to the box.

00:59:57.860 --> 01:00:00.897
This is 3.1 ounces, or 87 grams.

01:00:00.897 --> 01:00:02.265
Now we have the share size.

01:00:02.265 --> 01:00:03.600
Peanut makes its first appearance.

01:00:03.600 --> 01:00:07.270
This is 3.27 ounces, or 92.7 grams.

01:00:07.270 --> 01:00:08.237
Little bigger of a pouch,

01:00:08.237 --> 01:00:11.341
we have the 10.7-ounce, or 303-gram,

01:00:11.341 --> 01:00:13.343
sharing-size pouch part two.

01:00:13.343 --> 01:00:14.944
Then we jump up to the family size.

01:00:14.944 --> 01:00:18.214
This is 19.2 ounces, 545 grams.

01:00:18.214 --> 01:00:20.350
Throwing a party? M&amp;M's got you covered.

01:00:20.350 --> 01:00:21.517
This is the party pack.

01:00:21.517 --> 01:00:24.487
38 ounces, 1,105 grams.

01:00:24.487 --> 01:00:27.757
And the biggest portion
size you can get is this,

01:00:27.757 --> 01:00:29.993
the pantry-size tub.

01:00:29.993 --> 01:00:34.631
62 ounces, 1,757 grams.

01:00:34.631 --> 01:00:37.533
In the UK, M&amp;M's come in
four standard portion sizes.

01:00:37.533 --> 01:00:39.268
Around the holidays, you
can get a selection box

01:00:39.268 --> 01:00:41.871
with a small packet of
M&amp;M's that weighs 45 grams,

01:00:41.871 --> 01:00:43.473
but unfortunately, we
couldn't get one today.

01:00:43.473 --> 01:00:45.875
Our standard pouch is 125 grams.

01:00:45.875 --> 01:00:47.644
Then we move up to a more-to-share bag,

01:00:47.644 --> 01:00:50.713
which, for standard chocolate
M&amp;M's, comes with 250 grams.

01:00:50.713 --> 01:00:53.182
The largest size available
in the UK is a party bag.

01:00:53.182 --> 01:00:54.717
I went to about eight
different supermarkets

01:00:54.717 --> 01:00:55.718
and I couldn't find one,

01:00:55.718 --> 01:00:58.054
but usually they would
contain 1 kilogram of M&amp;M's,

01:00:58.054 --> 01:00:59.122
so we're going to make our own.

01:01:06.429 --> 01:01:08.398
There is our unofficial party-size bag.

01:01:08.398 --> 01:01:09.832
1 kilogram of M&amp;M's.

01:01:09.832 --> 01:01:11.467
All said, America's largest size

01:01:11.467 --> 01:01:15.038
is 75.7% larger than the UK's.

01:01:15.038 --> 01:01:17.140
In the UK, the portion
sizes also vary slightly

01:01:17.140 --> 01:01:19.275
depending on which flavor
of M&amp;M's you've opted for.

01:01:19.275 --> 01:01:22.311
A more-to-share bag of
chocolate M&amp;M's is 250 grams,

01:01:22.311 --> 01:01:26.015
but a more-to-share bag of
crispy M&amp;M's is just 246 grams.

01:01:26.015 --> 01:01:27.617
If you want the most value in the UK,

01:01:27.617 --> 01:01:28.685
opt for peanut M&amp;M's.

01:01:28.685 --> 01:01:31.921
A more-to-share bag of
those contains 268 grams.

01:01:31.921 --> 01:01:33.589
Are the M&amp;M's themselves different sizes

01:01:33.589 --> 01:01:34.524
in the UK and the US?

01:01:34.524 --> 01:01:36.459
We're going to weigh out
100 grams of chocolate M&amp;M's

01:01:36.459 --> 01:01:37.860
and count them to see how many you get.

01:01:37.860 --> 01:01:39.929
One, two, three ...

01:01:39.929 --> 01:01:42.165
Two, three, four, five ...

01:01:42.165 --> 01:01:45.101
[fast-forwarding]

01:01:45.601 --> 01:01:46.869
That is so annoying!

01:01:46.869 --> 01:01:49.005
It was so close to being 100 grams

01:01:49.005 --> 01:01:50.173
of exactly 100 M&amp;M's,

01:01:50.173 --> 01:01:52.508
but instead 100 grams
of UK chocolate M&amp;M's

01:01:52.508 --> 01:01:54.477
is 102 M&amp;M's.

01:01:54.477 --> 01:01:57.647
100 grams of American M&amp;M's

01:01:57.647 --> 01:02:01.017
is 114 M&amp;M's.

01:02:01.017 --> 01:02:02.652
So what does that mean, ours are smaller?

01:02:02.652 --> 01:02:04.153
And how do we feel about that?

01:02:04.153 --> 01:02:05.755
I don't know if it's better or worse.

01:02:05.755 --> 01:02:07.657
But portion size don't stop there.

01:02:07.657 --> 01:02:10.493
You can also buy M&amp;M's
directly from the M&amp;M website.

01:02:10.493 --> 01:02:11.661
The main purpose of this seems to be

01:02:11.661 --> 01:02:14.163
catering for large events
like weddings or parties.

01:02:14.163 --> 01:02:16.466
You can technically get
smaller-than-average portion sizes,

01:02:16.466 --> 01:02:17.934
but only in bulk quantities.

01:02:17.934 --> 01:02:20.336
For example, in the US, you can get these.

01:02:20.336 --> 01:02:22.772
Tiny party-favor packs of M&amp;M's

01:02:22.772 --> 01:02:26.075
weighing just 0.75 ounces each.

01:02:26.075 --> 01:02:28.344
Or they have party-favor tins,

01:02:28.344 --> 01:02:31.514
which contain 1.5 ounces of M&amp;M's.

01:02:31.514 --> 01:02:33.216
But both of these have to have a minimum

01:02:33.216 --> 01:02:35.551
of 20 or more units.

01:02:35.551 --> 01:02:37.954
Now, what doesn't require a minimum order,

01:02:37.954 --> 01:02:39.355
however, are the bulk bags.

01:02:39.355 --> 01:02:41.124
In the US you can order bulk bags

01:02:41.124 --> 01:02:44.527
of 1 pound, 2 pounds, or 5 pounds.

01:02:44.527 --> 01:02:47.029
Now, technically, you could
order 10 pounds of M&amp;M's,

01:02:47.029 --> 01:02:49.198
but they just send you two 5-pound bags,

01:02:49.198 --> 01:02:51.534
which is a bit disappointing,
so we just got one.

01:02:51.534 --> 01:02:53.202
5-pounder.

01:02:53.202 --> 01:02:54.303
Look at these M&amp;M's.

01:02:54.303 --> 01:02:56.172
The UK website is a similar situation.

01:02:56.172 --> 01:02:59.509
Our smallest portion size is
this 28-gram designer case.

01:02:59.509 --> 01:03:01.477
But the minimum order for these is 20.

01:03:01.477 --> 01:03:03.746
Unlike the US, we only
have one bulk-bag order.

01:03:03.746 --> 01:03:06.048
And that's this one,
which is 1.5 kilograms.

01:03:06.048 --> 01:03:09.218
That's around 3.3 pounds,
which is a 34% decrease

01:03:09.218 --> 01:03:11.454
from the largest single
bag size in the US.

01:03:11.454 --> 01:03:12.755
If you do order M&amp;M's on the website,

01:03:12.755 --> 01:03:13.823
you can customize them.

01:03:13.823 --> 01:03:15.258
We chose some custom colors

01:03:15.258 --> 01:03:17.426
and also put some custom
text on the M&amp;M's.

01:03:17.426 --> 01:03:18.561
In terms of colors, I went for this

01:03:18.561 --> 01:03:19.796
lovely blue-and-white color scheme

01:03:19.796 --> 01:03:22.064
to match my stunning M&amp;M's T-shirt.

01:03:23.099 --> 01:03:25.067
Then I had some fun putting
some text options on there.

01:03:25.067 --> 01:03:27.370
Firstly, I went for "Harry &lt;3 Joe."

01:03:27.370 --> 01:03:28.538
We also had to rep the show,

01:03:28.538 --> 01:03:30.173
so I put a "Food Wars" one on there.

01:03:30.173 --> 01:03:31.574
Then, because I have the mind of a child,

01:03:31.574 --> 01:03:33.376
I tried to put some
swear words on the M&amp;M's,

01:03:33.376 --> 01:03:35.278
and it turns out they
actually try and censor you.

01:03:35.278 --> 01:03:37.547
For example, if you try and
put the word "poop" on an M&amp;M,

01:03:37.547 --> 01:03:38.748
a warning message will flash up

01:03:38.748 --> 01:03:40.316
telling you to get in touch with the team.

01:03:40.316 --> 01:03:41.584
But there is a work-around.

01:03:41.584 --> 01:03:42.785
For example, for the word "poop,"

01:03:42.785 --> 01:03:44.687
by replacing the O's with 0s,

01:03:44.687 --> 01:03:46.022
I was able to get around the censorship

01:03:46.022 --> 01:03:47.356
and create poop M&amp;M's.

01:03:47.356 --> 01:03:50.526
The same goes for replacing
the I with a 1 in "penis"

01:03:50.526 --> 01:03:53.029
and replacing the A with a 4 in "balls."

01:03:53.029 --> 01:03:56.065
This is some serious journalism
taking place right here.

01:03:56.065 --> 01:03:59.302
Now, Harry, of course,
went with customizing M&amp;M's

01:03:59.302 --> 01:04:01.237
with fun words and stuff on it.

01:04:01.237 --> 01:04:03.306
I just went for pictures.

01:04:03.306 --> 01:04:06.075
You can get custom images on an M&amp;M.

01:04:06.075 --> 01:04:08.177
So what I did is I got

01:04:08.177 --> 01:04:11.981
Harry face and Joe face M&amp;M's.

01:04:11.981 --> 01:04:13.115
OK, that'll show 'em.

01:04:15.384 --> 01:04:18.287
Here are all the ingredients
in chocolate M&amp;M's in the UK.

01:04:20.189 --> 01:04:22.525
And here is everything in a bag

01:04:22.525 --> 01:04:25.528
of classic M&amp;M's in the US.

01:04:25.528 --> 01:04:26.996
Look at all those colors.

01:04:26.996 --> 01:04:28.030
A few things to note here.

01:04:28.030 --> 01:04:29.532
Firstly, the food colorings used

01:04:29.532 --> 01:04:31.300
in the two countries are wildly different.

01:04:31.300 --> 01:04:33.102
In the UK, some of our colors are natural,

01:04:33.102 --> 01:04:35.438
including the curcumin and the carotenes.

01:04:35.438 --> 01:04:38.608
Whereas in the US, all
our colors are artificial.

01:04:38.608 --> 01:04:40.943
Blue No. 1 is used in
both the US and the UK,

01:04:40.943 --> 01:04:43.813
but we also have Blue No. 2, Red 40,

01:04:43.813 --> 01:04:45.915
Yellow 5, and Yellow 6.

01:04:45.915 --> 01:04:48.117
Blue 2 is a less common one.

01:04:48.117 --> 01:04:50.553
It's also known as indigo carmine.

01:04:50.553 --> 01:04:52.922
Now, the good news is it won't
make your kids hyperactive.

01:04:52.922 --> 01:04:55.691
The more interesting news is that Blue 2

01:04:55.691 --> 01:04:57.927
is filtered rapidly through the kidneys,

01:04:57.927 --> 01:05:02.598
and consuming enough of it
will turn your pee blue.

01:05:02.598 --> 01:05:04.467
The practical use of this is so doctors

01:05:04.467 --> 01:05:07.536
can highlight your urinary
tract for surgeries.

01:05:07.536 --> 01:05:10.439
A less practical effect or use
is to freak out your friends.

01:05:10.439 --> 01:05:12.475
Hey-o, we're doing jokes
in the script, apparently.

01:05:12.475 --> 01:05:14.377
Hey, welcome to "Food Wars"!

01:05:14.377 --> 01:05:16.646
So anyway, turns your piss blue.

01:05:16.646 --> 01:05:17.647
Speaking of carmine,

01:05:17.647 --> 01:05:19.715
what about the carmine
used in British M&amp;M's?

01:05:19.715 --> 01:05:21.550
Standard carmine is a red food coloring

01:05:21.550 --> 01:05:23.819
with the code names Red 4 or E120.

01:05:23.819 --> 01:05:24.887
It's a natural food dye,

01:05:24.887 --> 01:05:26.822
but what is the natural source, you ask?

01:05:26.822 --> 01:05:28.157
It's cochineal beetles.

01:05:29.492 --> 01:05:30.860
If you grind up cochineal beetles,

01:05:30.860 --> 01:05:31.894
you're left with a red powder,

01:05:31.894 --> 01:05:33.663
which when mixed with
water and some chemicals

01:05:33.663 --> 01:05:35.364
can be turned into a very stable dye.

01:05:35.364 --> 01:05:37.366
Obviously, we're going to now
have to try and make our own.

01:05:43.940 --> 01:05:46.342
But you can see the red color
coming off of it already.

01:05:48.144 --> 01:05:49.812
Now I'm going to try and
put some of this in there,

01:05:49.812 --> 01:05:52.348
mix it with some water,
and see what happens.

01:05:54.083 --> 01:05:56.519
That has really worked. Wow.

01:05:56.519 --> 01:05:58.554
Look how red that is! That's incredible.

01:05:58.554 --> 01:06:00.022
As you can see, just by
chopping up some beetles

01:06:00.022 --> 01:06:02.058
and mixing it with water,
we've got this incredible

01:06:02.058 --> 01:06:04.026
kind of blood-red food dye.

01:06:04.026 --> 01:06:05.561
Now, while apparently
synthetic alternatives

01:06:05.561 --> 01:06:07.563
to carmine do exist, M&amp;M's confirmed to us

01:06:07.563 --> 01:06:09.799
that the carmine they use does
in fact come from beetles.

01:06:09.799 --> 01:06:12.668
So, technically, every time
you eat a red M&amp;M in the UK,

01:06:12.668 --> 01:06:13.903
you're eating bugs.

01:06:15.338 --> 01:06:16.772
So, do you want your kids hyperactive,

01:06:16.772 --> 01:06:18.874
or do you want them eating beetles?

01:06:18.874 --> 01:06:20.109
Not much of a choice, is it?

01:06:21.877 --> 01:06:23.813
Here are all the M&amp;M's
products you'll find in the UK

01:06:23.813 --> 01:06:25.381
